  ('zcrm_1579374000156310082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156781087', 'Christopher Cook', NULL, '1-8-25 They tried to create a C4 account but they don''t have her A-Number/USCIS number. It''s back in Japan. I was thinking the AC plans could work but we may have the same problem. So, now I think it''s best to go with MCS and it also works abroad. It will be much better. They are hoping to make $150K in 2025 as well. I just sent them the video to watch and we are meeting on Monday at 3:00. they in are Boulder until the 18th.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 16:47:15', '2025-01-08 16:47:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156310077', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156781087', 'Christopher Cook', NULL, '12-2-24 Hi Wendy,

So, as is the case on almost everything we are doing, there is a catch.   In this case, the catch is that the site for https://connectforhealthco.com/ won’t allow me to create an account without a US phone number. Sigh… And the Phone carriers won’t let me create a phone account until I have a local address. And the Rental companies want a local bank that needs a phone number and address….  So it seems all progress points to getting a lease signed with a Boulder address.  We will be coming for a visit to Boulder Jan 5th - 16th, so hopefully we can untangle this mess when we get there. Our intentt is to have a lease, phone, and bank account established early in that visit.

In the mean time I can answer a few questions.

1. We reviewed all the disclosure statements and we answered no to each. So at least that’s one non-issue

2. Since we are going to be spinning up our own business when we get there, annual income is a bit sketchy  but we are setting a target for 2025 of $150K of combined household income (Hopefully more) . So I think medicaid is not an issue. I also suspect, that no subsidy would be under that entry either but I’m way short of an expert.

3. Still concerned about how Medicare will play into this as we both turn 65 next year (July, and Oct)


Let me know if there is anything more we can do to move the ball in the near term.

Thanks

Chris & Missy', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 16:44:46', '2025-01-08 16:44:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156310072', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156781087', 'Christopher Cook', NULL, '11-27-24 Dear Wendy Scipione,

We were given your contact  info by Delphine Carlile who is helping us with our relocation to Boulder Co area. 

We have some unusual circumstances that we need to chat with a a specialist in US Health care coverage. We have been living for the past 9 years in Tokyo Japan operating our own consultancy company and insured for health matters under the Japan Health Insurance system via our consultancy company.  We are both US citizens on special Visa here in Japan but have had no need for US health care coverage over the past 9 years.

In Feb 2025, we will be returning to the US and will initially open a US corp to continue our consultant business so we will now need some kind of US Health insurance (perhaps under ACA)  to cover us both. To complicate matters, we will both be turning 65 next year (July and Oct) so Medicare comes into things somehow.

Let us know if you think you can help and if so, when we might be able to have a chat. Please note we are still in Tokyo at the moment so chat times are going to be a tricky matter to work out.


Thanks in advance for any help you can provide.

Chris & Misako', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 16:43:48', '2025-01-08 16:43:48'),
