  ('zcrm_1579374000156310031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156316001', 'Carlyn MontesDeOca', NULL, '1-8-25 Carlyn asked many more great questions, along with her husband. I described Premium Care until she tried enrolling and it''s not allowed in NM! UGH, I forgot. So, I re-explained the differences with CARE+ vs Premium Care. The price is a bit higher $352/$1000 and $107 = $459. She successfully enrolled for Feb. 1st start date and will cancel her ins for Jan. 31st. She also enrolled in HAB successfully for Feb. 1st, 2025. She''s all set to go and will schedule the Welcome call and save the Quick Reference Guide.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 12:20:08', '2025-01-08 12:20:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156310026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156316001', 'Carlyn MontesDeOca', NULL, '1-3-25 Carlyn, 63 (Sounds like Carleen) came to me via Krista Rogers. She watched the video. Lives in Santa Fe, NM down the street from Krista. Her husband Ken is in Medicare. She''s paying for PT 2x month $70. Yes, she wants annual wellness and likes holistic health. We discussed Premium Care and HAB $285+$107 = S392. She plays pickle ball and sees chiro for shoulder. Uses supplements and is excited for the 30% discount.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-08 12:17:09', '2025-01-08 12:17:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156254054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154723001', 'Madeleine McGuire', NULL, 'Member price was computed incorrectly at time of enrollment.  Spouse is already 30 and they paid the 18-29 rate for the month of 1/25.  I will email member &amp; advisor advising them of the $4 price increase moving forward.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-01-08 12:03:47', '2025-01-08 12:03:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156301104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061571018', 'Randy Sherer', NULL, '1/8/25: Randy called wondering why he hasn''t received any cards or emails etc after signing up. I resent him the Plan overview email and let him know that the fulfillment letter was sent yesterday so just give it a week or two - otherwise if he has anything come up, to give us a call. Set FU for 2 weeks out to check on fulfillment letter, txt review link. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-08 12:00:39', '2025-01-08 12:00:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156311071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109779071', 'Ruth Glas', NULL, '01.08.2025 ARM card vs Planstin - pharmacy benefits 30 days vs. 90 days.
PHCS search for PCP or NP on multiplan link: Will send info to Lori (Information is in Teams Chat). We talked about filling out the form for labs and prescriptions, in order to save money, PRIOR to purchasing. 
Mammogram was getting done at the Cleveland Clinic, but they are no longer in the PHCS network (confirmation from Julia came through on this YESTERDAY via Teams Chat). Ruth might still decide to continue with them, due to history and monitoring what her results have been. 
I sent Ruth two emails: The Preventive Care Resources & The refresher welcome call. She received both. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-08 11:54:48', '2025-01-08 12:19:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156311063', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000112836002', 'Andre Savoie', NULL, '01.08.2025 Andre wanted clarification on coverage for colonoscopy and the status of his HSA account. He called Planstin - needing information on a colonoscopy, and wanting to pay for it via HSA. Planstin told him that his HSA - has been dropped and that he needs to contact MPB.
We discussed if the colonoscopy is covered, and I went over the healthcare.gov ACA guidelines UNLESS they pull polyps that are concerning. THEN Zion will need to share in the diagnostic colonoscopy.
Andre seemed adamant that his next colonoscopy WILL NOT fall under the ACA guidelines, b/c in the past they did find something. I explained to him that it could still go through MEC ACA guidelines first.
Andre did seem a little agitated and tried to accommodate the conversation and his concerns, but I think he was worried about something else.
*********************************************************************
Andre called back asking to learn about other memberships that might have lower cost premiums/less benefits. AKA different memberships.
I was able to transfer him to Adam Jordano, after confirming via Teams Chat.  NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-08 11:53:05', '2025-01-08 12:51:44'),
