  ('zcrm_1579374000156097210', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012273725', 'Denise Matouk', NULL, '01.06.25:  Since I did''t hear back from Kelly, I messaged her a reminder to search Mailchimp for Denise''s change of price emails. Kelly found that Mailchimp had sent the emails to Denise''s old email, not her current email and said they bounced back. I asked Kelly to find out what Denise''s old email is, let me know , then change that email to her new email. JSP', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-06 15:56:27', '2025-01-09 08:22:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156159103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061924134', 'Kristen Lassalette', NULL, '01.06.2025 Kristen went for an preventive appointment in October 10.31.2024, provider called Planstin, 8889207526. According to Kristen the provider  spoke with Planstin said "they are not an insurance and will only reimburse the patient instead". Aspen Valley Hospital is out of network, but Planstin will cover, by reimbursement of $578. 
When we called Planstin, Karen answered, and she confirmed that Planstin told the provider that this is an insurance under the ACA guidelines. In network will cover 100% preventive services. If out of network, the options are that the provider bill the preventive coded bill to Planstin and they will cover it, RBP. 
The provider does not sound like they are will to bill. So Karen shared with Kristen her options then.
On 10.30.2023 Kristen had a prev. mammogram, Aspen Valley Hospital (same hospital), out of network, but Kristen then did not have RBP. Planstin did not pay.
Karen offered to do a courtesy call to the provider to submit the claim to them. Otherwise Kristen will pay the bill, request a super bill, and send it to the claims@planstin.com email. Karen will connect with Kristen after she''s talked with Aspen Valley Hospital to take the next steps for Planstin to reimburse. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-06 15:53:24', '2025-01-14 11:24:20'),
