  ('zcrm_1579374000156159058', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130194018', 'Christiaan Zaayer', NULL, '01.06.2025 Teri went to the doctor on 08.09.2024, took son to pediatrician for ankle injury - xray - referred to an orthopedic for fracture 08.13.2024 - also sports medicine orthopedist on 08.13.2024 - where they did more xrays. 
I explained that Planstin can send an EOB, denying all the claims, so she can proceed with the initial university insurance. Then we can open a Zion member portal, so she can open a sharing request as well on the same incident to be ready to upload all receipts showing she''s fulfilled the IUA and any remaining bills that need to be shared. 
We brought Planstin in, Caitlyn picked up, and she confirmed it was Wyatt not Brandon, who injured his ankle. That means they can send Teri the EOB, b/c he''s under 18 years of age. If it was Brandon, they would need to send the EOB to Brandon directly, due to HIPAA compliance. 
Teri might open a sharing request - she''s trying to get the 1st insurance to pay 1st. I told her it won''t hurt to open a sharing request, just so she''s not missing the deadline. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-06 13:32:06', '2025-01-06 13:49:08'),
