  ('zcrm_1579374000156016146', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013590075', 'Jason Adams', NULL, '01.03.2025 Created CRM task to confirm ARM card is delivered/sent to Jason. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-03 17:54:49', '2025-01-03 17:54:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156029053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156186015', 'Noah Burleson', NULL, '1-3-25 Noah and his wife have had their baby successfully! His wife was induced, had the baby, was discharged for 48 hours and then landed back in the hospital for spinal headaches. Now she''s seeing a psychiatrist every other month. It cost $300 for the initial visit and $150 for each additional visit. Since they live in CA, they need Secure HSA EF 18-29 for $776/$1000 or $638/$2500 plus possibly HAB $107 for wife''s mental health benefits and gym, etc. She wants to keep her psychiatrist ongoing. She''s dealing with delayed post-partum depression. I let them know anything abnormal with the pregnancy will be considered pre-x. He mentioned some labs were off, hence why I let them know about the pre-x in that case. They understand. Noah used to use a medication for sweating too much. He''s off of that now. He can use virtual healthcare app for stuff like that. He doesn''t have anything else of concern. They are paying about $600 per month right now, but clearly not happy with the coverage. They are paying the full cost of the psychiatrist as well. His wife''s meds are super affordable such as just a few dollars and same for his. I sent them the Maternity Guide, let them know pregnancy must occur after the start of membership, I copied the entire maternity section from the Sharing Guidelines and sent him the video to watch again. He''s an ASHI member and will get $100 waived!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-03 17:33:09', '2025-01-03 17:33:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156016111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155308040', 'Natalie Lawlor', NULL, '01.03.2025 SalesIQ chat - sent through Teams chat - 
1- Welcome email: nothing from MPB nor Zion - we did call Zion 3-way. Isabella sent her the welcome email from Zion.
2- MPB Portal access: Gave her access to her MPB portal. Isabella from Zion sent her the invitation link to open the Zion portal. 
3- CirrusMD registration: Had her set up all the adults in the family (Natalie, Jason, Elise and Emry).

IT about the MPB app - their identification/account did not populate for me to give her the credentials. Created a CRM Task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-01-03 15:58:09', '2025-01-03 17:58:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156029048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107787002', 'Nathan Smith', NULL, '1-3-24 Nathan was double billed. His membership was slated to begin on 1-1-25. However he was billed on 11-20-24 and 12-20-24. I submitted a tkt and Julia said that he''s been refunded now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-01-03 15:54:54', '2025-01-03 15:54:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000156029043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155863302', 'Kymberli Collins', NULL, '1-3-25 Bill called me back right away and gave me far more helpful information showing all of the screenshots and proof of why he believed their plan had successfully auto-renewed. He has a letter from Anthem stating the plan is not changing and can be auto-renewed. He has screen shots from Anthem on 12-12-24 showing the plan is set to auto renew for 1-1-25 effective date.  He also has a screen shot from Anthem on 1-2-25 showing his plan was successfully auto-renewed and is active as of 1-1-25. So, I''ve updated the request to Broker Team for the escalation and this is their response, 

Hello Wendy,

The action below in the customer account Opted out of the Renewal.

However, there is an open Case # with the Back Office for review. Please wait for the Back Office to respond to you.

