  ('zcrm_1579374000155905076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000135183021', 'Larissa Brice', NULL, '12.31.2024 Needs to change the payment information with MPB. I led her to the form. She submitted it successfully. It is in the "Update Form of Payment" Cognito file. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-31 16:02:42', '2024-12-31 16:02:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155905068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011881581', 'Jason (Jay) Wright', NULL, '12.31.2024 IN the CRM Profile - Nahla changed the "Add on Product" information from Planstin to ARM. I attempted to send them their cards, since I do not see an email sent out from here, but their cards are missing from the list that ARM sent. There isn''t any Jason Wright at all in the list of PDF''s. 
Meghan emailed us via Concierge email regarding how to get reimbursed for an out of network OBGYN visit. I emailed her back with the following answer:
"...It is great to hear from you! I am not sure if you received my message through Jason''s phone, regarding the issues we discussed. I will put my findings all in here then.
Starting with the out of network preventive appointment with your OBGYN;
It is strongly encouraged to maintain the PHCS-Practitioner and Ancillary network, in order for ARM to maintain the low prices. From what we learned, out of network services could be covered, if the following are practiced:
The appointment is coded PREVENTIVE by the physician
The claim is billed to ARM directly by the physician
What happens when the member pays for the appointment, and pursues reimbursement, is that ARM cannot process with the discounts and the member may or may not get fully reimbursed. To send the bill to ARM, please use this email address: kait@altrisk.com..." 
I also included the information from the last bullet notes I have on the 23rd of December. 
- MPB ID cards
- MPB Portal Access
- CirrusMD registration.              NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-31 15:40:28', '2024-12-31 16:07:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155916001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144228001', 'Cynthia Franceus', NULL, '12-31-24 Cynthia joined Delta Dental Clear Plan for $63 per person. She has dental needs to take care of right away. Her dentist accepts many insurance plans such as Aetna (but didn''t show up in 1Dental), Ameritas, Anthem, Some Cigna, Delta Dental, Guardian, Metlife, UHC, United Concordian. The Clear Plan with Delta Dental will give her benefits immediately without the typical limitations. She signed up and it will begin 1/1/25.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-31 15:37:03', '2024-12-31 15:37:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155824996', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156321001', 'Brianne Davis', NULL, '12-30-24 Brianne is 44 and her  kids are 17, 14, and 12. She has 2 step kids that are on their own plan already, I believe. She lives in Boulder, CO. She works with Jessica Muniz as a nurse in alternative care style facility. She wants to be finished with traditional insurance. She sees no value in those anymore. They are all healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco. Two of her boys have ADHD but take generic meds. She does wellness, dental, vision, mammo and alternates with themogram, usually needs the additional ultrasound, gym for club soccer, ski pass, etc., mental health off and on, labs and skin check. No vax or nutrition. Her late husband was killed 8 years ago!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-31 15:30:23', '2024-12-31 15:30:23'),
