  ('zcrm_1579374000155824914', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000149941002', 'Brian Erickson', NULL, '12.30.2024 She was in the ER last week, gall stones,  is having surgery this Thursday 01.02.2024 to remove them. Kindly guided her to to connect with Sedera, since they really like having the hands on approach when it comes to opening and processing the medical needs. I suggested she call them and tell them she was in the ER last week, and having surgery this Thursday. I gave her Sedera''s number. I will create a CRM Task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-30 15:47:49', '2024-12-30 15:56:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155824909', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000089510002', 'Tyler Farrish', NULL, '12.30.2024 Bria called to open another maternity sharing request. She could not access her Zion mbr portal, so I just reminded her of the TYPE of sharing request to choose, once she''s in. As well as, paying her IUA from the sharing request, once it''s deemed shareable. I transferred her to Zion. I opened a CRM Task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-30 15:43:02', '2024-12-30 15:43:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155835079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129625123', 'Casey Zahorik', NULL, '12-30-24 Casey got bitten by a dog and is having trouble finding an in network dr. They wanted to use UC Health but those aren''t in network. Select Health is the best for UCH this year. I let Kim know that now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-30 15:33:51', '2024-12-30 15:34:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155835071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152284778', 'David Spear', NULL, '12-30-24 Shelby called bc she received a 2nd letter from Medicaid saying the whole family qualifies for Medicaid which is opposite of what C4 shows. It''s telling her if she has both Medicaid and C4 with APTC, she will have to pay full price for her C4 RMHP. She''s clearly not able to do so. Her income is on the cusp of Medicaid vs APTC. But, C4 shows Sophie might qualify for Medicaid. Shelby and David qualify for APTC of $1858.33. To avoid paying full price, she just cancelled PMHP. She doesn''t work with an accountant. She''s afraid of having to pay back her APTC for Dec. since Medicaid is now telling her she qualifies for Medicaid. However, she''s been following the instructions from both systems that don''t seem to be functioning properly or talking to one another. I''ve never seen this happen. I suggested that she calls Medicaid to see if they have a glitch or incorrect information on their end.  She''s super frustrated and I don''t blame her. Her account seems to have a problem with it!  She''s done everything in her power to keep her account accurate per the instructions provided to her all along.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-30 15:20:36', '2024-12-30 15:22:33'),
