  ('zcrm_1579374000155824202', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106861002', 'Timothy Sadusky', NULL, '12.30.2024 Connie called per Planstin''s request, to better learn how the changes of her MECs is going to affect her and the colonoscopy she has scheduled in January. I told her that NOT MUCH changed from Planstin to ARM, other than:
- Where the claims need to get sent
- The sub-network in PHCS from Specific Services to Practitioner and Ancillary
- Dermatology Screening - (PURELY Looking)
We went in depth of how to bill ARM, and that she can contact us if she needs us to advocate for her to get the provider to bill ARM. We also we into depth on how large medical bills are usually handled. Connie is not very comfortable with how the preventive is limited and her lack of knowledge on the healthsharing portion makes her uneasy as well. I gave her a tiny example on how healthsharing is more efficient than traditional insurance by using PRE-X condition tiers from Health Sharing entities vs. ZERO coverage from traditional insurance.
I offered her to receive an orientation call with Vanessa to better understand the details. She was very receptive to that idea. 
I sent her Three emails: The preventive services, The ARM card and the welcome call. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-30 12:17:49', '2024-12-30 12:17:49'),
