  ('zcrm_1579374000155589233', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155415021', 'Anthony DeLuise', NULL, '12.24.2024 Anthony called to get help in changing his passcode for the MPB portal. I helped with that via Admin123. He successfully accessed his MPB Portal, with the new passcode. He asked what are some items to prepare for, give his welcome call is not till later. I responded to register for CirrusMD. His credentials did not take yet, given his start date in a couple of weeks, but I put in a ticket anyways to CirrusMD - just in case. He wanted more information on MEC+Essentials - Julia, via Teams Chat, suggested the Member Handbook. In search for that member handbook - asking if there''s a NEW CONCIERGE PLAYBOOK link to re-add to my resources. ......', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-24 09:36:50', '2024-12-24 09:36:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155619463', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000116616002', 'Cora Lonning', NULL, '12/24/24: Cora emailed in the following question in response to receiving her her MEC card:
I have questions. 
I specifically went with a non-traditional health care option (Cost share) to avoid being on the Government marketplace AND being restricted to the marketplace network. My sole intention is to be able to see the doctor of my choice. 
If I am reading this correctly, I have been put back in the marketplace, which limits me to the providers IN the marketplace network. A nightmare I do not wish to revisit. 
 
Please advise if I am reading this correctly. 
If I am now on the marketplace for preventative care I will need to review my options .

Replied with the following response:
The plan that you have includes medical cost sharing for large, unexpected medical expenses – and there are no network restrictions for medical cost sharing.
 
Your plan also includes a MEC (Minimum Essential Coverage) for preventive care. This MEC is what qualifies you to be able to contribute to an HSA account. This small part of your plan is contracted with the PHCS network.
 
I hope this clears things up. If you have additional questions, please let us know.
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-24 09:28:30', '2024-12-24 09:28:30'),
