  ('zcrm_1579374000155355490', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601365', 'Matt Holstein', NULL, '12.20.2024 Matt called to get help in getting his colonoscopy covered. His screening/surgery was on 07/23/2024, when he was still with RCI.
I called ARM to see if they can see him in their system, and they can. They also saw claims from that service that they are working on getting paid. 
Lori from ARM shared that they received the claims on 12/11 and processed on 12/17.
They check runs once a month.
She shared that the anesthesiologist got paid, and cashed his check, and that the bill for $1221 is the facility bill.
What Lori thinks could be missing is the surgeon''s bill. 
I called Matt back and let him know about ARM having the claims already and waiting on more, given the possibility of missing the surgeon''s bill. Also to call back the facility and make sure that all entities BILL ARM and erase RCI. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-20 15:27:53', '2024-12-20 15:53:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155385053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000155863212', 'Hillary Thomas', NULL, '12-20-24 Hillary asked many questions that I answered. She has a number of meds that we discussed all of which she believes are generic. They cover mental health, skin, water retention, sleep, thyroid and weight loss/longevity and for constipation. She understands pre-x and IUA. She has a Concierge Dr. that she really likes. So, HAB is excellent to take care of anything else preventive and is ultimately only $54 more bc $124-$70 reimbursement = $54 and Premium Care is $285/$1000, $125/$25. MPB on Amex and HAB on checking account. Hillary came to be via Alicia Turbidy and she added her on the app. Tracy Matthews handles all of her banking and paper work. Hillary is in CA now on trip but lives in FL. SHe recently had a full body scan and everything looked good! No tobacco, no other pre-x other than what she manages with meds mentioned above. She prefers alternative drs. and care nowadays. She has a therapist that she seems sometimes that she can use HAB for reimbursement. She also does mammo every year and MRI follow up every other year. She goes to yoga and pilates classes as well. She''s enrolled for Jan. 1st. Tracy will make sure Hillary is cancelled for her Anthem plan for Dec. 31st as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-20 15:21:14', '2024-12-20 15:35:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155385048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045841172', 'Shoshana Kressler', NULL, '12-20-24 Enrolled in Premium Care $1000/$837 and HAB $250. All set for 2025! I waived the $100 fee since they were members with PDHC in the past.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-20 15:17:08', '2024-12-20 15:55:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155382124', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131740002', 'Anzhelika Siloyan', NULL, '12/20/24: Called Planstin to check status of member. William informed me that she was activated this morning at 7am. He checked with Zion to make sure everything was showing in their system and Zion wouldn''t tell him anything. William sent an email to Zion making sure they are aware of the update. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-20 14:53:23', '2024-12-20 14:53:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155385043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130526354', 'Sondra Blanchard', NULL, '12-20-24 Sondra''s price is going up quite a bit $569 or so to $700+. We reviewed options. She was bummed that she missed the Dec. 15th deadline which she didn''t know about. She was interested in going back to MCS but she had some menstrual issues and small possibility of surgery. It''s all well managed for now but not worth the risk if that changes this year. So, we looked at a Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $7200 to give her co-pays for Dr. visits, labs, urgent care etc. Her current Kaiser plan is $6500 ded and covers nothing until she spends that much. So, for slightly more $ she will get some valuable benefits. Her income is $101,364 or so for 2025. APTC is $241.61.  I also priced out Anthem Bronze Pathway Essentials 8000 for HSA which would be $341.91 her cost vs $432.79 for  Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $7200. So, she''s thinking the $90 savings per month isn''t worth a plan that offers nothing until you reach $6500. She will ponder and we will connect again in early Jan.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-20 14:26:13', '2024-12-20 17:48:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155385038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130802017', 'Bruce Maleski', NULL, '12-20-24 Completed Change Form to Convert from Secure HSA to Premium HSA for Jan. 1st, 2025. Chose $2500/$587 EG.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-20 14:17:28', '2024-12-20 15:57:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000155355485', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000135149007', 'Timur Zamaletdinov', NULL, '12.20.24:  Called Tim - l/m to c/b. Explained the 2025 plan price increase. Suggested he stay with his plan. Had a slight increase of $8/mo.  Told him to call me w/any questions.   JSP', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-20 13:58:24', '2024-12-20 13:58:24'),
