  ('zcrm_1579374000154873046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060125007', 'Michael Remacle', NULL, '12-17-24 Secure HSA EC $1000 going from $650 to $733 as of 1/1/25. If drop MEC it will be $627+$200 HAB = $827.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-17 16:17:07', '2024-12-17 16:17:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154873041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148858973', 'Karl Hill', NULL, '12-17-24 I sent Karl the HAB flyer and showed him how to submit his hockey bill for reimbursement. Sounds like he''s already submitted his wellness screening before as well. He''s getting the hang of it. All set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-17 16:12:29', '2024-12-17 16:12:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154873036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060125007', 'Michael Remacle', NULL, '12-17-24 Michael is interested in doing his preventive colonoscopy this year and possible heart screening. I let him know ACA plans don''t include cardiology testing. ACA compliant wellness are all the same no matter what plan he chooses. I shared HAB with him in case that serves him better moving forward. He will review it. They will keep Kyle on his current Secure membership to work towards getting reimbursed for costs. They were very pleased with Acelyn''s help also. I recommended Michael calls Rachel and really presses Zion for answers as to how to break out the various Needs moving forward, so they will begin sharing! Apparently Acelyn also sees how Zion thinks one Dr. was for mental health not physical health bc that Dr. has two separate practices and Zion must have looked at the wrong one. They also wanted to know the cost of C4 plans and they are about double the cost and then $18K mop. Kyle can qualify for Medicaid since he''s filing his own taxes now. He''s not earning any money right now. If Zion won''t pay then he can get on Medicaid and they might also help pay some of his bills from the 3 months prior to qualifying for Medicaid.  They will press on for Kyle. Their daughter Lauren will be graduating from CU in May and may need a plan at that time. We looked at the cost of adding her to C4 and it was about $400 per month. Not worth making a change until she graduates.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-17 16:10:59', '2024-12-17 16:10:59'),
