  ('zcrm_1579374000154885023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000137206002', 'Richard Hirsch', NULL, 'Member submitted Change Form to add newborn Richard Hirsch to membership.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-12-17 12:28:40', '2024-12-17 12:37:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154899086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012010011', 'Elizabeth Wood', NULL, '12.17.2024 Elizabeth called trying to figure out how to get her claims covered. There''s a discrepancy in her timeline and the information provided. Presently she does not have any MEC with us AO 11/1. Her HAB through Wendy kicks in then, and that''s her preventive care.
In August 2024, we learned and practiced/processed that RCI members are to be transferred to ARM instantly by 09/01/2024. Elizabeth is sharing that she had RCI till 10/31/2024. This is news to me, and so I checked with Julia via Teams chat to confirm, and she confirmed that RCI members were to switch to ARM by 09/01/2024.
However Elizabeth''s interaction timeline shares differently. She has bills that need to be covered (the fact that the MEC was not billed directly is a WHOLE SEPARATE situation, and should be addressed ONCE WE LEARN WHO EXACTLY IS/WAS HER PREVENTIVE CARE in September and October). 
Elizabeth called RCI, after she had TWO preventive appointments in October. Went to doctor 10/15/ & 10/31. $8K lab work claims!!
RCI referred her to ARM. I had no idea RCI was still answering member calls by then. Given OUR EXPERIENCE and calling them.
ARM shares that she is eligible, and is willing to put her as eligible eff 11/1. ARM is about to send her an ID card, she''s in their system.

Was she on ARM in Sept and Oct?

Messaged Wendy to clarify a bit, and Wendy shares that "She had RCI up until Oct. 31st and then we removed the MEC for Nov. 1st. Someone messed up somewhere bc RCI is showing she was cancelled in Aug. which is not true."

According to Julia - we stopped paying RCI August 2024.
Called ARM and asked if she indeed was in their system since 09.01.2024. I spoke with Dave, he confirmed that she was on HDHP - high deductible plan - her enrollment of 9.01.2024 till 10.31.2024. 
I called Elizabeth back to direct her to email Kait@altrisk.com with all her claims. I followed up with a text from GoTo.
Starting a CRM task to follow up - NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-17 12:28:38', '2024-12-17 14:26:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154885018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919234', 'Casey Hebb', NULL, 'Received Change form to add newborn to membership (1st notification).  We were not informed by Sedera.  I will add newborn to the membership.  No change in price since already a family.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-12-17 12:21:28', '2024-12-17 12:21:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154885013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113416002', 'Conrad Buteau', NULL, 'Member submitted Change From to add newborn Rosemary the membership.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-12-17 12:07:13', '2024-12-17 12:07:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154899003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100491002', 'Michelle Faciana', NULL, '12.17.2024 Michelle called to get help in deleting her old form of payment. I messaged Patti, while she was still on the phone with me, and Patti was able to delete the old one instantly.
Michelle proceeded to ask questions about her membership details, especially with the price increase, the difference in the MEC PHCS networks, between Planstin and ARM, and if at all possible would Zion share in Celiac disease.
We went over in detail the difference on how to present via MEC appointments, and cash pay visits, as well as searching for providers in the Practitioner and Ancillary Network with ARM, and how keeping it in network helps keep the costs low. 
We discussed that I would do some search on possible Zion sharing into Celiac disease, as well as what the umbrella title would be for her sharing request be, instead of allergies.
I will create a CRM task. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-17 12:02:56', '2024-12-17 12:09:17'),
