  ('zcrm_1579374000154872016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154438001', 'Holly Wielsma', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on vm. Told member to reach out to us and I can schedule a welcome call after available hours after her start date of January 1, 2025. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-17 11:43:59', '2024-12-17 11:45:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154873018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '12-16-24 After sharing this story with the Advisors, they are not pleased at the response. We can''t know all the areas of the country that are deemed "expensive" in the medical industry. Telling clients they might have to pay for half of a $50K surgery will not fly. So, we are setting up a meeting to discuss further.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-17 11:39:25', '2024-12-17 11:39:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000154873013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044486166', 'Elizabeth Collins', NULL, '12-3-24 Here''s Juliet''s response regarding Liz'' 2nd knee surgery.

Also, thank you for reaching out about Liz''s case. I read through all of the communication in this thread. I also know how challenging it has been for the community with members in the mountains in Colorado. The Steadman Clinic has done an outstanding job of monopolizing the market there, having incredible marketing, and making it seem that they are the only choice for treatment. By doing so they are able to have incredible inflated costs. I was actually just speaking to a potential group up in the same area. The owner had recent treatment at Steadman clinic and wanted to know how this would be shared. I had to bring up the same Guidelines that the Needs Coordinator did in this thread with Liz. While we do have freedoms of networks at Sedera there is a huge responsibility we all share in finding fair priced providers in our area or slightly outside our area while Sedera shares in the cost of travel.

If all of our members chose to go to the doctor of choice with extremely inflated costs, we would not be able to function as a community. Our costs would exceed the monthly contributions and we would have to close our doors. This is a member responsibility we take very seriously due to the ramifications we would see if everyone didn''t abide by the rules. 

I always try to look for ways to assist our members and fight for them if I think there is any way around what they are experiencing. Unfortunately, there is not going to be a different outcome on this one. All members need to understand that we are in this together. It''s different from insurance. 

When speaking to future members in the Colorado area, I suggest bringing this up as part of the conversation. They are making a choice to live somewhere where medical costs are highly inflated across the board. If they are up for traveling to attain a fair price for the community, then Sedera could be a great option for them. If they are not willing to travel or seek out fair prices with our resources, Sedera may not be the best choice for them. 

I''m happy to jump on a call to assist and connect further on this one. I will always do as much as I can for you and your members."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-17 11:38:02', '2024-12-17 11:38:02'),
