  ('zcrm_1579374000154689003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027924354', 'Darrin Hallman', NULL, '12.13.2024 Darrin put in an RX request, shortly before he called in for:
1- Entresto: 97mg/103 mg - 60 Tablets (to take twice a day for 30 days)
2- Farxiga: 10mg - 30 tablets
He has a heart issue, he''s passed the pre-existing condition mark, has a pacemaker, has individual market place insurance (pays first for the pacemaker, then Sedera kicks in), takes 2 medication per month (~$700 each).
THAT insurance is going up to $1200 a month. Checking in to see if it is worth keeping it or can he let go of it.
Does not want to get stuck with ~$120k bill for a pacemaker in 5 years, biggest concern is the cost of the medication (been getting help with the other insurance on that) - in the past....

Trying to sign up with CitizensRX, but their log in to their member portal is down. Will check with ARM then CitizensRx.
While on the phone, he did see on the Sedera website that they ALSO have international pricing.

As of now, Darrin is leaning towards feeling comfortable with letting go of the marketplace insurance, given the assistance attached to the said medications, BUT HE STILL wants to learn if Sedera would share in for a pacemaker in the next 5 years.
I will connect with Sedera to generate some bullet points for Darrin and the team. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-13 10:30:50', '2024-12-13 17:13:49'),
