  ('zcrm_1579374000153984026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078467032', 'James Fontenot', NULL, '12.06.24:  Called Barry to let him know that we have a plan that is less expensive than the increased rate of Care Plus  and also has some preventive care services - Premium Care, w/Sedera. He was interested in possibly changing to this plan. I emailed him my website link to review the details of Premium Care, as well as the link for the Sedera plans change form. Told him to contact me before he makes any changes and reminded him of the 12/20, 3 p.m. deadline.', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-06 12:47:59', '2024-12-06 12:47:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153967094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919617', 'Heather Davies', 'New Membership eff 1/1/25', 'Member Only $5000 IUA Premium HSA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-12-06 12:41:55', '2024-12-06 12:41:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153967089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919617', 'Heather Davies', NULL, 'Member submitted Change Request to change to the Premium HSA membership eff 1/1/25.  I will process', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-12-06 12:41:17', '2024-12-06 12:41:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153917079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993452', 'Holly Wiese', NULL, '12-6-24 Holly and Greg had many great questions about their membership and submitting a new Need for Greg''s hand injury. He just had an x-ray today or yesterday and might need PT and who knows what else. I told them to call the MPB Concierge Team to open the Need and start tracking the cost. They are also interested in HAB but are weighing the value vs losing the HSA tax benefits. Holly needs an MRI following her mammo from May or June and wants to know if she can use that to get the MRI reimbursed in Jan. Tanya Dueri had asked before but her mammo was about 8 months old already and HAB wanted a new mammo to pay for the follow up. She was also asking about a colonoscopy and the cost. I looked up Colonoscopy Assist and she can get it for $1475 in Loveland, FC, Greeley or Denver, not in Boulder. So, she''s considering doing it in Boulder before she drops the MEC. Their new SECURE HSA membership will be $733/$1000. If they drop MEC and add HAB it will be Care+ $627 + $200 = $827 or $2500/$520 + $107 = $727.  She was also curious cost of keeping MEC $733+$200= $937. They will talk with their accountant to make a decision. They might choose to wait a month or two to fund their HSA or get colonoscopy first.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-06 12:36:32', '2024-12-06 12:36:32'),
