  ('zcrm_1579374000153881182', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002724127', 'Paul DeFelice', NULL, '12.05.2024 Paul and Karen called earlier around 2CT. Sharing that the facility they went to get the colonoscopy at was not going to bill Planstin, saying they are not in the network.
Initially, when Paul and Karen went to the facility, they were going to get charged $500 for a consultation fee which I then informed them that it would be out of pocket. They then went through their physician and got a referral, Karen''s name made it through the referral but Paul''s did not. Paul said he will take care of that on his end.
They proceeded to share that after they went through the process of getting the referral to have the procedure, the facility now is saying that they are not in the PHCS network, and will not even bill Planstin through the RBP price model. Karen and Paul were really good about repeating the tools to the facility to guide them through the process, but the facility is not wanting to participate. 
Unsure why they state they are not in the network, when more than 6 of their doctors are named in TWO PHCS networks: Limited Benefit Plan & Preventive Services Only.
I called Planstin and spoke with William, who explained to of course double check with the providers and facilities to confirm if they indeed are still in the network, given how many exit the network and do not clean the list (removing themselves). However this would have been brought up PRIOR to Paul and Karen going to their physician to attain a referral.
William also gave me the PHCS phone number to call and confirm with them, and possibly learn of any options from here. 
I offered to call Paul and Karen back this evening. I will but I still do not have a solution. They will hear from me some more tomorrow. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-05 16:16:43', '2024-12-05 16:16:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153917024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136256011', 'Brian Coffey', NULL, '12-5-24 Brian called because he spoke with Medicaid today and they say he''s qualified until May of 2025. He''s not allowed to have a APTC and Medicaid but they seem to have their wires crossed and he has both. To avoid any problems in 2025, we had him cancel his Cigna plan and he will keep Medicaid until he receives the official letter kicking him off of Medicaid. He knows to call me at that point and we''ll get him going again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-05 16:09:58', '2024-12-05 16:09:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153881172', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000096327002', 'Lucas Battista', NULL, '12.05.2024 Tried calling Lucas back, but got his VM again instead. LVM. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-05 15:26:55', '2024-12-05 15:26:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153883050', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165427', 'April Porterfield', NULL, '12/5
Planstin rep called with the member on the back line. The rep and member claim that MPB misinformed the member about coverage of the bone density. With that being said planstin wants us to fix the issue because it was we who misinformed the member and they do not want to pay the bill AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-05 15:23:58', '2024-12-05 15:23:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153881167', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117650002', 'Paul Copeland', NULL, '12/5/24: Susan Copeland asked if we could help her find an Integrative Spec. in network. I let her know that there is no network. We attempted searching HCBB, but was not successful finding drs like that through them. She already had a spec. in mind so we left it at that. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-05 15:06:27', '2024-12-05 15:06:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153883045', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129016002', 'Paige Anderson', NULL, '12/5
Paige called to ask how to open a sharing request for her husband''s eye surgery. She also wanted to see if to was eligible for sharing I reviewed the guidelines and it looks like they are good to go.  AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-05 15:05:52', '2024-12-05 15:05:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153917019', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165420', 'Jennifer Shedd', NULL, '12-5-24 Jenny wants a plan around $300 with lower ded and mop. Her income is higher and is totally open to MCS again. She can''t get what she wants through C4 with her income. Plus it''s so sporadic. She''s getting penalized for last year bc it was higher than she thought. She has migraines and takes meds when needed. She saw a neurologist for it recently and they just suggested some meds. She''s had the problem since she was 13. So, she''s not worried about anything changing.  She has very well managed type 2 diabetes which she mostly handles with diet, exercise and low dose metformin which is about $10. She was thrilled to rejoin with MPB and Sedera at $285/$1000 since that''s exactly the budget she was hoping for. Then she uses ALL of the wellness benefits for HAB. So, she decided that makes sense to include as well since she''ll probably win on the financial aspect of that and can keep her providers. She''s also interested in learning about becoming an  Advisor.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-05 14:31:17', '2024-12-05 16:31:14'),
