12/04/2024', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-04 20:36:57', '2024-12-04 20:36:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153758064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154585008', 'Nicole Boye', NULL, '12-4-24 Nikki is 51, Erik 55, Ian 23, Logan 21 and Ellie 19. They came to me via Cory Nickerson. They live in Boulder, 80303. They earn around $300K and still can get a tiny APTC. That''s insane! Two kids take SSRI''s that are cheap. Nikki takes metformin. She said her A1C is 5.6 which is in the normal range. But, she''s still doing things to make sure she''s not pre-diabetic. She takes generic Synthroid and hormone meds. Two kids see a therapist every two weeks. They want to keep Lauren Kaiser PA and Dr. Hillary Wallace for main Drs. Due to mental health needs, I shared HAB and they would use wellness screenings, dental, vision sometimes, gym for ski pass and pelaton, mental health, labs, vax, just no for nutrition. Nikki sees a functional medicine Dr. in Louisville. They are paying $1800 now which also includes vision and dental. I quoted her Premium Care $1000/$837 + HAB $250 = $1087 or $1500/$741 +$250 = $991. Two kids are out of state for school. One is in UT and the other, I''m not sure. All 3 might be out of state next year. So, ACA is too complicated. They''d need 4 different plans for their entire family. She''s interested in 1Dental for kid who''s in UT for Sugar House Dental is in the Dental Access network. Dr. Anja Mohelicki is not in network which is her dentist here in Boulder. She does accept Delta Dental but that''s $126 per month for just the two adults. The prices are insane all of the sudden. I told her to save up money for dental and skip the insurance. They also use supplements and like the 30% discount on those. She will review it all with her husband, including the video. She watched the video already.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-04 20:14:39', '2024-12-04 20:14:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153758059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000136256011', 'Brian Coffey', NULL, '12-4-24 Brian is guessing his income will be about $40K minus about $5K in expenses. So, we plugged in $35K and he gets a $476.10 APTC. I sent him some plan options. The 2nd cheapest silver plan or cheapest silver plan (I forget) actually looks the best, especially since he''s not tied to any dr. right now. He''s temporarily living between Estes Park and Lyons but keeping his current address. He''s also not sure how to handle his daughters who are currently on Medicaid. We left that alone so they don''t get bumped off. He will handle tax stuff later. His youngest sister who is 49 is close to passing away. She begrudgingly gave in to taking the shot while working at Barklay''s since peer pressure got to her. Now she''s in renal failure, had sepsis, eyes are yellow and she''s jaundiced. She started with neuropathy in her legs 1-2 years ago. Now she''s on dialysis and is given 72 hours. Even after asking NOT to be given Remdesivir, the seemingly gave her that as well and put her on a ventilator. She''s sadly doomed. Brutal!!!  This comes after his mom died also soon after taking the shot. 
He will look over the plan options and let me know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-04 19:57:19', '2024-12-04 19:57:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153758054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045841172', 'Shoshana Kressler', NULL, '12-4-24 I adjusted Sam''s income to $180K and yours was in there at around $7700. There was another small deduction you had in there from before which I left. So, the total is showing $187,565.88. With that you get a modest tax credit of $56.83 per month.&nbsp;I sent them 6 options to review.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-04 17:59:17', '2024-12-04 17:59:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153777100', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000117456002', 'Kelly Pieropan', NULL, '12.04.2024 Jennifer called back to offer the update on attaining her bills/invoices from the providers regarding the endoscopy. She kept on getting the run around, and telling her that she can get it from her chart.
Her chart was not working, so she contacted IT.But IT did not get back to her. She will contact them tomorrow, giving this another try to attain what she needs to upload all bills prior to her cancellation. 
I sent her the cancellation form via CRM. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-04 17:53:08', '2024-12-04 17:53:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153777095', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146467002', 'Meegan Oldani', NULL, '12.04.2024 Meegan received the script email.
Meegan goes 1/year for Zantac visits that cost around $500~, and wants to see if CirrusMD would be willing to let her go the route of telehealth, as long as she''s seeing someone in person. I explained that detail to her, and to be ready for a possible no, due to it being a strongly controlled medication.
Also she messaged Zion RxShare - but they have not responded to her. She will inquire about the medication she''s currently on, as well as her son.
She will try telehealth tonight to introduce herself and hopefully discuss the above situation. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-04 16:50:41', '2024-12-04 16:50:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153777090', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740129', 'Julia (Wieck) Hardy', NULL, '12.04.2024 After chatting with Wendy via Teams Chat, I learned that Julia would like some guidance in opening those sharing requests with Zion. I called her to offer my guidance and 3-way call to Zion, Julia said she would love to do that, but does not have the time. She shared she will spend the time this weekend to gather all the bills/invoices from all the providers in mind/on hand, and open the sharing requests next week. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-04 16:35:15', '2024-12-04 16:35:15'),
