  ('zcrm_1579374000153664013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000115751002', 'Rocio Borzage', NULL, '12/4/24: Sent FU email to William letting him know what I found out from Cirrus:
Here’s what I’ve learned so far:
1. Your eligibility has been updated in their system, and your account should now appear as active.
2. Regarding the removal of medical records:
    * If this pertains to prior encounters with providers, they cannot delete those records while maintaining your access to your children’s accounts.
    * However, there is an option to completely remove your account and all associated records through the CirrusMD app. In the app settings, you''ll find an option labeled "Delete My Account," which will deactivate your account entirely.
I also asked if it might be possible for you to delete your account and then reactivate it without the previous records, but I’m still waiting for confirmation on that.
AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-04 07:41:11', '2024-12-04 07:41:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153664008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025283259', 'Julie Oldham', NULL, '12/4/24: Julie called. She said over course 6 months she''s had issues with uterine hyperplasia, and cannot have biopsy, now needs hysterectomy. - does she need pre approval for surgery? She''s already started sharing request. I ended up connecting her with Sedera just in case. 
