  ('zcrm_1579374000153587134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134767002', 'Kara Weld', NULL, '12/3/24: Kara emailed into info email asking how to access HCBB. Provided universal login. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-03 17:53:47', '2024-12-03 17:53:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153585138', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000066564305', 'Robert Mitchell', NULL, '12-3-24 They still get a huge APTC and we just need to pick the plan with most of the Drs.  We will discuss on Friday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-03 17:03:22', '2024-12-03 17:03:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153587118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000029000272', 'Katelyn Doty', NULL, '12/3/24: Katelyn called asking if we could help her find a decently priced psychiatrist. I attempted to do a quick search with the tools we usually use and didn''t get very far. Offered to ask some people in the office in the morning to see if we could offer any resources and get back to her. AM

Some options based on research: sent email
Brightside.com > Virtual psychiatry plans - $95/month (maybe available visit by visit basis)
Sondermind.com > Self pay rates between $53-$200/session
Sesamecare.com > Visits seem to be around $150/session
American Psychiatric Association > finder.psychiatry.org > offers a comprehensive lists of psychiatrists in specific zip codes', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-03 16:47:11', '2024-12-03 17:45:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153585133', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000151131001', 'Jackson Lebsack', NULL, '12-3-24 Linda realized Jackson can qualify for ACA. I thought I could help them until I now see he''s in OR, not CO. Assuming he doesn''t claim residency in CO, they will have to find someone local to help him. Ugh! He makes about $26K per year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-03 16:44:11', '2024-12-03 16:44:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153587103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114408002', 'Anthony Nelson', NULL, '12/3/24: Emailed Allison Imaging Quote results. See Images and Email for info. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-03 16:26:11', '2024-12-03 16:26:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153587098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114408002', 'Anthony Nelson', NULL, '12/3/24: Allison called with questions about billing. She''s had a knee issue for a while and has already paid $2100+ towards the issue since April. I advised her to go ahead and open her sharing request right away and to speak with Zion about any services she''s had that might not be eligible anymore due to 6 month deadline. She is needing to get an MRI but wondering if she should wait till January or do it now (She was under the assumption that her IUA starts over in Jan) -I educated her on how IUAs and sharing requests work. She''s been pricing options for MRI. I offered to perform a search for her to see if I could find a better price and emailed Imaging Quote form. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-03 16:24:44', '2024-12-03 16:24:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153585128', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154195001', 'Robynn Browne', NULL, '12-3-24 Robynn is 58 and husband 57. They were referred to me by Stacey Wiley and her husband. They live in McCall, ID. Her husband had a heart attack at age 49 and he''s been good and on meds ever since. However, he chimed in and says he has Coronary Artery Disease. So, we should keep him on trad ins. I''m looking into to seeing he he will qualify for America''s Choice. Nevermind, I looked it up and it''s considered heart disease and he''s taking meds for it. So, I don''t think it''s a good idea. He needs an ACA plan on his own in ID. Robynn has macular degeneration in her eyes. She will need to decide if that will be a problem with the pre-x clause. They are paying $2600 now on Cobra!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-03 16:12:33', '2024-12-03 16:12:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000153585123', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153586188', '(Boyce) Ben Ford', NULL, '12-3-24 We removed Mary Geitner (Ben''s now e-wife) from the membership and Willoree his daughter. He claims Phoebe every year and Mary claims Willoree every year. That might change in 3 or so years when Phoebe goes to  college.  Ben makes about $37,016 according to his last taxes which he thinks will be close.  He''s a contractor and writes a ton of his expenses off. He''s getting a $485.48 APTC. His cost is only $38.42 with $100 ded and $850 mop. He''s thrilled. Both daughters are on CHP+ already. He knows to call to set up auto pay in 10 days.  This is set for Jan. 1st, 2025.
We also enrolled him in 1Dental since we found his dentist in the network. He joined for Dec. 1st at $99+$20.  He''s all set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-12-03 15:39:36', '2024-12-03 15:39:36'),
