  ('zcrm_1579374000153425028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010282165', 'Alicia Turbidy', NULL, '12/2/24: Called Alicia in response to the VM about flu shots she left last week. She said she spoke to someone but they weren''t able to tell her anything.
According to Sedera''s guidelines, flu shots are shareable. The member just needs to submit an itemized bill for reimbursement. Tina at Sedera verified this for me. 
Alicia is planning to go to CVS to get shots for her and family. 
She also asked where her daughter could go for a dr in NY or should she just use Cirrus. I explained to always start with Cirrus if she can bc that is available with your plan and she can use it as often as she likes. Otherwise, she can go to any dr and submit sharing requests like usual no matter which state she is in. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-12-02 08:24:15', '2024-12-02 08:24:15'),
