  ('zcrm_1579374000152766033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152759099', 'Brandy Mortashed', NULL, '11-22-24 Bev''s client, Michael Gardner, Brandy''s husband is offered health ins through his county job. They pay 100% of his cost. They offer it to Brandy and it would cost her around $360. So, she doesn''t qualify for a tax credit. She was getting a substantial tax credit it 2024 which she may be penalized for when they file their taxes. She is going through treatments, chemo, etc. right now. They are afraid to change their plan. They''ve already met the ded and mop. He knows to fund the HSA. To keep the same plan it will cost $580.62. I told him to try to get her onto his employer plan. He doesn''t know when their open enrollment is. He will want to make sure she can keep her doctors in-network if they switch. They also wanted to keep their dental plan. I selected both for them. His income changed from $38K to $51K, therefore household income went from $50K to $63K for 2025. Her income is $12K both years.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-22 14:02:06', '2024-11-22 17:53:31'),
