  ('zcrm_1579374000152693023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152427002', 'Traci Gervase', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to reschedule welcome call after start date of December 1, 2024. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-22 08:32:48', '2024-11-22 08:32:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152693013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142357002', 'Sara du Toit', NULL, 'Spoke to member will reschedule welcome call after December 1, 2024. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-22 08:08:21', '2024-11-22 08:08:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152666013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000077566026', 'MaiLan Boris', NULL, '11/22/24: MaiLan emailed asking if her upcoming colonoscopy can be counted towards IUA if polyps are pulled. (See full email below). Sent her an email (look in email section here) giving her guidance on how to proceed. Advised her to present planstin card for billing, and if they pull polyps and it is then coded as diagnostic, she can submit as a sharing request to Zion. AM


_______________________________________________________________________________________
 Good morning,
I am still very confused on how to proceed with the upcoming colonoscopy''s billing. 
My August required consultation in order to schedule the screening procedure has a Balance Due from the Provider (via PHCS).  This amount was notated as a part of my deductible, which I don''t with PHCS!
The colonoscopy has been coded as "family screening" by the PA for PHCS.  The provider had explained that if there are polyps to be removed then it will be billed as a surgical procedure-- so the coding is a to be determined item ...

My question is:  if this happens, would the balance due that I am being hounded for BE COUNTED TOWARDS THE AMOUNT OUT OF POCKET WITH ZION?  And what do I do when I get the billing from the providers, which will be HIGH because it went thru insurance billing this NO Cash Amount could be negotiated for now!!!

Please advise.....as I don''t want to get caught in the middle after paying into the Sharing Plan all of this time !!!!
Thank you.
Mailan Boris', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-22 07:31:22', '2024-11-22 07:31:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152666003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108524001', 'Megan Land', NULL, '11/22/24: Megan called asking if she would see the price increase come out of her acct in December or January. Let her know it''d be December. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-22 07:10:39', '2024-11-22 07:10:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152601104', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163576188', 'Daniel McCarthy', NULL, '11-21-24 Dan is 64 and wife 60 or 61. Came to me via Bev bc she hasn''t turned off her contact info from C4 yet by accident. He''s looking at plans that cost $2100-$2400. They get an APTC but cost will still be exhorbitant for 2 people. He was looking at the RMHP HSA or a non HSA plan. The HSA plan is more expensive than the other Bronze plan he was comparing it to. They are both mostly healthy. He needs to see an eye specialist in 6 months to check his eye. He might possible need an retinol eye surgery. His wife has asthma that she manages well with meds. They also use the following for HAB, dental, vision, gym, skin, vax, labs, mammo and mental health. they are all set for colonoscopy for many years now. It makes most sense for them to do Premium Care $575/$1000 and HAB $100 = $757 and $125/$25. They could easily save over $1000 per month, $12000 per year to cover any unexpected costs. Dan will research MCS and I will send him video, and written overview.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-21 20:24:18', '2024-11-21 20:24:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152621082', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144862002', 'Alexja Cummings', NULL, '11.21.2024 Alexja has been trying to connect with us since yesterday. She apparently called 3 times yesterday, and kept getting a weird dial tone.
