  ('zcrm_1579374000152601096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152571065', 'Debra Nehlig', NULL, '11-21-24 Debra is a member with Middleway Wellness / Mary Ellen Franscescani. If she chooses Cobra it will cost her about $800 for medical, dental and vision. If she goes to Marketplace it will be $800-$1200!. She''s already paying for Middleway Wellness. She joined Care+ $352/$1000 and HAB $107 = $459 for Jan. 1st. effective date.  She knew about Mary Ellen''s husband as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-21 16:09:52', '2024-11-21 16:09:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152601088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130064059', 'Chris Gangwish', NULL, '11-21-24 Chris had his income at around $41,300 or so. But, he''s looking at 2024 which he made far less and expects the same for 2025. His estimate is $13,850. So, I plugged in the new income amount and he should hear from Medicaid soon.  This will likely go into effect for Jan. 1st, 2025. I put his account as Inactive since he will be moved to Medicaid for 2025.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-21 16:04:41', '2024-11-21 16:17:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152601083', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003413005', 'Jennah Synnestvedt', NULL, '11-21-24 Jennah is interested in life ins for herself only. We''re looking at 20 YR Term $150K max for around $25-$30 per month. She wants to stick as low as possible. But, she also has $175K debt and about $50K-$80K income. I ran it at Standard Non-Tobacco and hoping she''s rated better. She has great health, no meds, no tobacco, parents still alive and only minor health issues. Both had possible cancerous spots removed from skin and that''s about it. She has good credit at about 711. Her spouse Juan is 37, almost 38 and DOB 1/2/87. He can join Zion without SS#. She wants Zion also since she found their Essential prices are much cheaper and she doesn''t use any of the other benefits that MPB uses. 30-49 direct w/ Zion is $340/$1000 for ES. She''s paying $234 now. We will switch for Jan. 1st effective date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-21 16:01:58', '2024-11-21 16:01:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152601078', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000083756038', 'Lisa Birkhofer', NULL, '11-21-24 Lisa expects to make about $35K in 2025 which removes her CSR. Now her MOP is $9200 up from $100 which was a shock. She chose the Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 in case anything bad happens this year. She landed in the ER last year for getting hit in the head with a golf ball and needed 3 stitches. She''s still paying that off from the ER visit. Urgent care was closed. She was still bleeding even after they stitched her up. The golfers ran away. She also got bitten by a tick in the NE and got antibiotics. Otherwise, she''s super healthy and still mtn bikes and such. She has Delta Dental and VSP. She''s get an APTC of $916.56.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-21 15:54:05', '2024-11-21 15:54:05'),
