  ('zcrm_1579374000152443102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107134002', 'Thomas Beaudin', NULL, '11.20.24:  Recvd. an email from Thomas. He apologized for the delay in responding to my email. Said he would be happy to do the member commentary video but he may be cancelling his plan because he expects to change employment at the end of this year. If this happens, he will be closing his business, so he wants to know what the process is to cancel.  I emailed  him that I would be sorry to lose him as a member but I wish him success in his new endeavor if it happens and I''d still like to do the video interview with him.  I suggested a day in early December to do the video. I also told him all he needs to do to cancel is complete our cancellation form which I will send him a link for.  JSP', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-20 14:24:24', '2024-11-20 14:25:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152389064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610208', 'Marc Krawatsky', NULL, '11/20/24: Member called asking about ARM versus Sedera. I let her know that this is really a conversation for her advisor, but if they have an HSA account, they would want to stick with a plan that has a MEC like Planstin or ARM - it''s what qualifies them to contribute to an HSA. Member is going to reach out to advisor. In the meantime, need to ask Nahla if these doctors were brought up to ARM directly to see if they will pay claims from them. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-20 14:09:29', '2024-11-20 14:09:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152378186', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152485001', 'Todd West', NULL, 'Member  Fam MEC + Essentials', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-11-20 14:05:34', '2024-11-20 14:05:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152443070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091292', 'Carl Cheetham', NULL, '11.20.24:  Met with Carl today. Explained the following plans:  Premium Care, Care +, Premium HSA, Secure HSA and compared Direct with Premium Care. Sent him the link to my website so he could review the details of each plan, as he''s not sure which one he will go with.  He said he does have an HSA, so he may want to take one of our HSA plans to be able to continue to contribute to it.  If he changes his plan it will be for 1/1/25.  Told him to contact me with any further questions.  JSP', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-20 14:03:19', '2024-11-20 14:04:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152378181', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152395039', 'Natalie Hughes', NULL, 'Member Only $2500 IUA Secure w/ARM', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-11-20 14:01:03', '2024-11-20 14:01:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152443062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447148', 'Marie-Christine Carel', NULL, '11.20.2024 Mari-Christine emailed me via Outlook, inquiring about vaccines via Planstin. I sent her the following:
"Hello Marie-Christine,

So good to hear from you!
I''d be happy to break down your options in vaccine services right here.

With Planstin, who you have for your MEC services till the end of December, will cover the flu and covid shot. They are not covering the RSV as of yet. 
To be sure to get covered for the flu and covid shots, they must be done at the provider''s office and coded preventive. It has become clear that in order to be covered, vaccines need to be done at pharmacies, and the pharmacy needs to bill Planstin medically NOT pharmaceutically. We have recently learned that most, if not all, pharmacies are not able to do that. Therefore, that is why it is best that it is done at the provider''s office/visit, where they can bill Planstin under the term medically. 

I hope this was helpful. I will be here till 8pm, ET if you have additional questions. "    
*************************
Sent the following correction:
"My apologies! By fixing my grammar, I changed some statements that need rephrasing. I will do that here:
"It has become clear that in order to be covered, vaccines need to be done at pharmacies, and the pharmacy needs to bill Planstin medically NOT pharmaceutically." 
***In order for Planstin to be able to cover vaccines done at pharmacies, the pharmacy needs to be able to bill Planstin medically and code it preventive. Not bill pharmaceutically.***"     NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-20 13:37:39', '2024-11-20 13:45:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152441044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142370033', 'Michael Llerandi', NULL, '11-20-24 Mike chose to keep his Premium Care membership over his employers plan since they were so terrible. His new employer will give him a stipend to help pay for this!  We reviewed all that''s included and to contact MPB Concierge for most items for pricing and support. They aren''t good candidates for HAB since they really only need dental and vision. I let him know about the 6 month wait for mammo and colonoscopy. He did his 1 year ago and not sure if wife needs it. His dentist is not in 1Dental network so he''ll use his HSA to pay for dental. I sent him the VSP Choice Plan A or B option to review for vision. All set to move into 2025.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-20 13:26:34', '2024-11-20 13:26:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152443057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091168002', 'Rebecca Bernard', NULL, '11.20.2024 She is going for a skin care appt, possible cancer removal/biopsy, and wanted to learn how does her membership benefits fit in.
