AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-19 17:46:08', '2024-11-19 17:57:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152227136', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152299092', 'Melissa Starowitz', NULL, '11/19/24: Worked up a presciption quote for Melissa per request for Bupropion HCL XL. However I''m not sure if it''s correct so sent Melissa an email asking if Generic Wellbutrin is what she is looking for. From what I researched, wellbutrin is bupropion hydrochloride. Will follow up tomorrow if I don''t hear back via email. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-19 17:41:04', '2024-11-19 17:41:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152227131', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000095868002', 'Joshua Platt', NULL, '11/19/24: Joshua submitted a custom lab quote with no info. Sent email requesting he re-submit with lab name. CRM shows email has been opened. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-19 17:14:29', '2024-11-20 06:58:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152298155', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152311057', 'Daniel Richardson', NULL, '11-19-24 Dan is enrolling now into Premium Care $1000/$285 and HAB $107 for Jan. 1st, 2025.  He is stepping down from his job as planned and is ready to roll for Jan. Very nice and all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-19 16:30:12', '2024-11-19 16:36:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152227121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061021001', 'Nathan Schultz', NULL, '11/19/24: Maya called with questions regarding two possible sharing requests:
1) She has an extra bone in feet that is wanting removed.
2) Lipedema - genetic mutation
I pulled up guidelines to see if there were anything that might be unshareable. While I didn''t find anything, encouraged Maya to review them too and emailed link.

Advised her to go ahead and open sharing requests for both issues, even if she doesn''t have all the details yet -  that way Zion can determine whether or not they are shareable expenses prior to scheduling surgeries. We went over paying IUA, how Zion pays out, submitting a good faith estimate, and sharing caps depending on how issue is categorized. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-19 16:18:21', '2024-11-19 16:18:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152298150', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032064012', 'Monica Rodriguez', NULL, '11-19-24  I sent this to her, "The cheapest plan won''t cover anything until you spend the deductible of $7500. The next plan Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $7200 gives you co-pays for Dr. visits and a few other items. But, for ER you pay 50% coinsurance after you spend $7200 for the deductible. The Cigna Connect Flex Bronze 0 gives you co-pays for most items which can help for Dr. visits, labs, imaging, urgent care, etc. There''s also a $1500 ER co-pay."  She has a recent ER vist for her son just a few days ago and doesn''t know the cost. I just let her know if she wants to get reimbursed, she will need to have her account active.  We will talk tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-19 15:00:24', '2024-11-19 15:00:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152298140', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032064012', 'Monica Rodriguez', NULL, '11-19-24 Monica Rodriquez submitted a cancellation form. She has no idea how to use her membership. She used the MEC card and never got reimbursed for any of her expenses, even those that exceeded $1500. I''m going to look at insurance with her tomorrow. She had an MRI a yeaar ago that cost her $2000. She had some gyno visit that was $800 and some other visits that she didn''t feel like sharing. I''m not sure if any of them are related or not. But, she''s going to have a brutal awakening when we look at health insurance!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-19 14:41:32', '2024-11-19 14:41:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152326225', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152342030', 'Jennifer Torres', NULL, 'Member Only $5000 IUA Secure w/ARM', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-11-19 14:28:06', '2024-11-19 14:28:06'),
