  ('zcrm_1579374000152298115', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000158474173', 'Stacey Gilmore', NULL, '11-19-24 Stacey wanted to see if she has the best plan or not. She''s paying $257 with Philly Life Insurance that has a health ins plan called First Health Network. She pays cash for everything and gets reimbursed. She has a $500 deductible! She thinks it might be nationwide since it''s based in Houston TX. She has an auto immune disease which she needs to see a rheumatologist, functional medicine Dr. She pays cash to both of these. She uses a derm and runs through ins. She also had a heart issue April 2021 which she had an ablasion done bc the electricity of her heart was off. An ablasion means they burn a part of her heart. She had super ventricular tachycardia and also sees an electrophysiologist and cardiologist. She takes a med off and on for this. Her body doesn''t absorb salt properly. So, when she''s feeling run down she takes the med to avoid any problems. This all started before she took the covid vax. She''s not a good candidate for MCS anymore with the heart issue, etc. She is interested in HAB, especially for the mental health.  She does get ACA compliant annual wellness screenings through her ins. She will review the brochure and let me know if she wants to join.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-19 09:38:58', '2024-11-19 09:38:58'),
