  ('zcrm_1579374000152298053', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143664002', 'Mary Ellen Francescani', NULL, '11-18-24 I requested removal of Jerry from HAB and awaiting response. It will be EO at $107. She didn''t include the kids.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-18 20:13:18', '2024-11-18 20:13:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152298048', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000110552002', 'Sheryl Hadley', NULL, '11-18-24 Sheryl is interested in HAB. She''s paying $375 now and will be paying $419 for Jan. 2025.  She could drop MEC and go with CARE+ $352+$107= $459, if she chooses.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-18 17:32:49', '2024-11-18 17:32:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152297101', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152321002', 'Zachary Lamkin', NULL, 'Enrolled in Secure HSA on 11-18-2024 $1K-IUA Family membership.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-11-18 17:26:31', '2024-11-18 17:26:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152298043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152320002', 'Stephanie Watson', NULL, '11-18-24 Stephanie and Zach chose CARE+ $1000/$672 and HAB $250 = $922 for 2025 and $1000/$635+$250=$885 for one month of Dec. 2024. They will keep their Cobra dental and vision. They will use the gym, wellness, skin check, labs, mental health, etc. It''s still worth the cost and they get to keep their drs.  They are all set to go for Dec. 1st effective date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-18 17:12:35', '2024-11-18 17:12:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152297096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146489002', 'Anna Nadasdy', NULL, '11.18.2024 Anna messaged back today regarding getting her vaccines at the pharmacy, King Sooper''s, who wanted to charge over $700. Anna then inquired, since the Urgent Care next to her is in the PHCS network (Prac. &Anc), can she go there and get her vaccines there.
I forwarded the email to Julia and Joan to help inquire about this in detail with me, and to possibly include it in the newsletter, to better educate the members. 
Julia responded via Teams saying to search for pharmacies in network, to use this site: https://discount.citizensrx.com/.
I still needed an answer regarding the Urgent Care option, so I called ARM back and asked. Lori said to veer away from trying to get vaccines at an Urgent Care. Furthermore, to see if the member can connect the pharmacy, when they are in network (like KING SOOPER''s), with CitizensRX and ask for Masha. Masha requested this specifically to help educate the pharmacy attendant/Nurse Practitioner there, on how to proceed with the billing appropriately to be covered by ARM.
I called Anna back, and worked through the above details with her. She was even familiar with Masha in the past, so she will reach out to her. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-18 16:05:34', '2024-11-18 16:05:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152227071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144870002', 'Aubrey Winik', NULL, '11/18/24: Resent quote and coupon per emailed request from Aubrey. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-18 15:06:35', '2024-11-18 15:06:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000152297088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108862002', 'Mark Witt', NULL, '11.18.2024 Mark responded to my email, in detail, regarding his wife''s on going visits to oncologist, cardiologist and pharmacy visits.
So recapping, in October, oncology initial appointment, was for the pap smear from the OBGYN.
While in ER for heart attack, the doctors saw the results for that.
Then found blood clot in lung, and is now on blood thinner > need a new sharing request
At the time they made biopsies in 5 locations.
They showed she needed additional tests: MRI on 11th, CAT14th
From MRI they found the blood clot - contacted the cardiologist and collaborated with oncologist - discussed type of blood thinner that ranged around $1000, with a discount ~$700. Eventually they spoke with the doctor''s office, who was able to provide them with a major discount to $10.
I contacted Mark back at home at 269-408-1748, where we went into detail on the sharing request requirements and if another one is needed for the blood clot.
I guided them to monitor the blood clot situation, and further services are rendered, then open another sharing request, unless the MRI has already reached the IUA.
I also explained our options in helping them save on the prescriptions, and the oncology medication can go under the sharing request. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-18 14:56:20', '2024-11-18 18:01:40'),
