  ('zcrm_1579374000151836121', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152320002', 'Stephanie Watson', NULL, '11-13-24 Stephanie came to me via Kristen and Steve LePeau through Porch Light Real Estate. Small world! Stephanie forgot that I do insurance as well. Hahaha! Zach is coming off of life long large group ins and is used to really good plans. Cobra was going to be $2500 a month. They were quoted US Health for $850. I told them to stay away from all of the bad stories I''ve heard. They were looking at some other option at $1100 which included dental, vision and medical as well as a Cigna for $1400. They don''t have any pre-x, no meds, no tobacco other than Stephanie taking hormone replacement therapy.  They are frequent users of urgent care for the kids. They landed in urgent care at least 8-10X this past year for injuries and strep throat, etc. So, with that in mind, they might be best served putting the kids on regular ins. and the adults on MCS. I sent them plans to review. Income is about $325K but fluctuates of course bc Stephanie is a realtor and you never know what the market will do. For Drs. that they want to keep, it''s Dr. Juliar, Dr. James Gottlieb, Dr. Hale (Derm) and Dr. Peart. None of the C4 plans have all of the Drs. in network. I suspect they can skip Dr. Hale for the kids. 
For MCS I quoted them CARE+ $1000/$672 and HAB $250 = $922 or SECURE HSA $1000/$780, $125/$25. I will now also quote them ES Only without the kids CARE+ $1000/$461 or Secure HSA $1000/$578,  HAB ES $200.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-13 20:10:54', '2024-11-13 20:10:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151888057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000128422001', 'Doug Shaw', NULL, '11.13.2024 Doug could not access his MPB Portal. I tried the present credentials successfully, and shared them with him, and he was able to get in successfully as well. We are not sure how the credentials changed, since he was using previous ones just fine, then all of a sudden, according to him, it stopped working. Unsure if the new website settings reset members'' credentials. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-13 17:25:47', '2024-11-13 17:25:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151836116', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000148475239', 'Michele Westmoreland', NULL, '11-13-24 Michele''s husband is diabetic and his drugs look to be very expensive and not covered by Cigna or anyone. Rybelsus and Jardiance 25 mg are super expensive. Amlodipine Besylate 5 mg is generic and affordable. She will speak with his Dr. to see if there alternative meds he can use instead. She is deciding between Cigna Connect Flex Bronze $0 and Cigna Connect Flex Gold. They are only $2 different in price bc of APTC. It''s looking like Bronze $0 is better bc of labs, imaging, PT, ER. So, the meds is the determining factor. She will send me a message once she knows.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-13 17:01:26', '2024-11-13 17:01:26'),
