  ('zcrm_1579374000151747125', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000151764180', 'Michelle Ruyle', NULL, '11-12-24 Michelle called and chose the RMHP Monument One Silver Advantage ($0 Virtual Urgent Care, No Referrals, $5 Tier 2 Rx, Rx Copay).  She is self-employed and is earning about $27-$30K, the least she''s ever made. So, she''s happy to have good benefits at a super low price now. She''s basically paying for it from her savings. It was $51 or so in 2024 and it will be $81.20 in 2025. She wanted an HSA compliant plan until she understood that nothing would be covered until she spent the entire ded first. So, she decided to keep her current plan. Acct #5810788270.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-12 19:46:17', '2024-11-12 19:46:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151747120', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060844140', 'Kevin Pfaff', NULL, '11-12-24 Laura and Kevin called bc Kevin can get ins through his work. We were thinking of moving Laura to Premium Care and have her just pay for the small wellness items. However, once they shared with me that Kevin has open needs for skin melanoma, it might not be best to move him anywhere. He''s had a number of spots removed. Each are around $900 to $1200. They''ve spent $4200 already. He submitted the Need 1 1/2 months ago. I recommended that they reach out ASAP to see what the determination is. If they share all of the ones above $1000 then he might have met 2-3 Needs already and won''t have to continue paying for additional spots. If he moves he''ll have a $7K ded and $9K mop to face. The plan through work is Anthem BC/BS PPO. It would be a little cheaper bc his employer is paying part of it but again he''d be liable to start over with his Needs. Then it makes more sense to leave Laura on the same plan in case she has any Needs, she won''t have to start over with her own 3 Needs. They will do their homework on their end. HAB didn''t seem worth it. They won''t use most of it. No for dental, vision, gym, nutrition, mental health.  If they remain on SECURE HSA into 2025 it will be $733/$1000 ES. If Kevin moves to his employer plan then we''ll move Laura to Premium Care $285/$1000 and she''ll pay for the smaller cost wellness visits on her own.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-12 19:27:12', '2024-11-12 19:27:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151747112', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033574061', 'Shawna Sands', NULL, '11-12-24 Shawna had to reschedule her wellness appt bc she didn''t have her ins card today! She''s super nice about it and she now has the digital card and is hoping for the hard copy as well. I''ve communicated with the Admin team to find out what''s happening.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-12 17:01:11', '2024-11-12 17:05:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151747107', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058247082', 'Anne-Marie Marron', NULL, '11-12-24 Anne-Marie enrolled in HAB w/ DPC for Jan. 1st start date already. We need to cancel MPB CareZ for Jan. 1st and re-enroll in Premium Care for Jan. 1st to bring down her cost as illustrated above.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-12 16:53:48', '2024-11-12 16:53:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151747102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058247082', 'Anne-Marie Marron', NULL, '11-12-24 Choosing to add HAB w/ DPC and her total additional cost is only $54 after the $70 reimbursement for being a Cloud Medical client.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-12 16:50:24', '2024-11-12 16:50:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151786046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043491580', 'Francis Lanzano', NULL, '11/12/24: Francis returned my call from Friday. He asked if he could get reimbursed for 9 therapy sessions and gym membership. I let him know that it''s a no on the gym membership, and MSEAP has not reimbursed in the past, however, if he''s interested in seeing the therapist again, he can go through the steps to see if they will join the MSEAP network. Francis isn''t interested in doing that now, but maybe in the future. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-12 16:30:47', '2024-11-12 16:30:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151786041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060844140', 'Kevin Pfaff', NULL, '11/12/24: Laura called asking what their pricing would look like if she were removed from the plan. Transferred over to Wendy. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-12 16:04:28', '2024-11-12 16:04:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151747097', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001637239', 'Dean Dealy', NULL, '11-12-24 Dean doesn''t have work right now. So, he''s wanting to lower his payment from $500 to $250 while he''s not working or for 3 months.  
Per Mara,
"His minimum is $166 a month so $250 will be fine for a few months and then if he wants to catch back up for his own benefit he can do a lump sum or increase his monthly amount. Either way. 

