  ('zcrm_1579374000151688006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144155002', 'Bethany Walsh', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request eff 12/24.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-11-12 07:49:26', '2024-11-12 07:49:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000113410109', 'Jeremy Colbert', NULL, '11-11-24 Jeremy is happy with his plan and I suggested for him to keep it. There''s nothing better than this plan still this year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 21:14:08', '2024-11-11 21:14:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008372009', 'Adrianne Middleton', NULL, '11-11-24 Adrianne needs  IV Gammaplex that looks to be over $500 cash price. It doesn''t show up in C4 at all and Cigna says it''s not covered. I suggested she talks with her Dr. to find out her options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 21:07:25', '2024-11-11 21:07:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643047', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752368', 'Jill Fields', NULL, '11-7-24 Jill is 51, interested in HAB for herself and possibly for her entire family even though Freedom Life.  They don''t have any wellness benefits. She will talk with her husband.  SDHC 50-59 $1000 IUA is $333. If she adds her family it will be $863. If they add HAB for EF then it''s $1113. Patti says they can make the change for Jan. 1st.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 19:47:00', '2024-11-11 19:47:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151603102', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000108211002', 'Karen Sachs', NULL, '11.11.2024 Karen needed extra guidance on how to move past "We have never heard of Planstin" when making a prev appt. She searched the multiplan link and found providers, but is having a hard time making that appointment. I coached her on how to proceed, and offered to work with her with them. I gave her extra information on the network titles and what to expect Jan1.2024. Karen is delightful and very receptive. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-11 17:55:03', '2024-11-11 18:14:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643042', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044061129', 'Emily Kloser', NULL, '11-11-24 Emily is very interested in HAB. They are also looking at joining a Functional Medicine Dr. for $5K per year for unlimited access, labs, etc. I''m guessing this can qualify as DPC. She also knows about Callie and Cassie Means!! She and her husband run bike tours in Europe. They have gotten their son to thrive again after serious gaming addiction, pot smoking, etc. He''s now working a good job, socializing, etc. He may be bumped off Medicaid any time and she thinks CARE+ will be good for him. 

If they drop Redirect it can look as follows, the newly monthly contribution will be $900.65.  They are paying $768.28 + cc fees = $785.15. To complicate matters, if you choose to join the Functional Drs. program, I suspect it will qualify as a Direct Primary Care - DPC which means your monthly cost would be $936.65 but you could then get reimbursed $140 per month for the DPC membership. This brings your monthly contribution back down to $796.65. 

She will review and let me know.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 17:46:14', '2024-11-11 17:46:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152460004', 'Sharon Montini', NULL, '11-11-24 Sharon found me via C4 in Louisville.  She watched the video for MCS and decided it''s not right for her. She is having some stomach issues and might need a gastro and possible colonoscopy or endoscopy. She'' had ulcers and hiatal hernia. She also has high blood pressure. She wants to keep Dr. Zara Frankel and Dr. Nuzhat Iqbal. If she has to choose, she wants to keep her gastro Dr. Iqbal. She may choose Anthem Colorado Option Gold Pathway Essentials Std with an $1875 ded. It''s the lowest ded to bring down the possible cost of procedure. She''s having stomach issues after last week, possibly election related nerves. She put her income at $94,300. Her husband Brent is on Medicare, 5-28-59. Her DOB is 10-25-61. She doesn''t want Kaiser for sure. She will review every plan and let me know which one she chooses in the next few days.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 16:58:07', '2024-11-11 16:58:07'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151603097', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000106720002', 'Jessica Chariton', NULL, '11.11.2024 Jessica called to get connected with her processor at Zion, regarding the sharing request she has open with them for her son Ridge. 
Jessica did seem on edge, and sounded like she''s been trying to connect with whom she thinks his name is Brian, her processor. She did not have his direct number, so I explained that they usually send email with their information on there, but I''d be happy to connect her with Zion so they can fulfill that request for her. I asked her if she would like it if I do a 3-way call with her or transfer her. She was quick to answer just transfer me. Right before I transferred her I coached her to press the number 6 for sharing request. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-11 15:50:29', '2024-11-11 15:50:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001538301', 'Brenda Smith', NULL, '11-11-24 Brenda was my client years ago with LHS. She came full circle and called Andrea who now referred her back to me.  Andrea didn''t help her yet.  Brenda thought we''d never spoken before. I found her here and confirmed she was a LHS member long ago. She is self-employed and wants decent hospital coverage and Dr. visits. She was recently with Tru Health but discovered she didn''t have great benefits. She had Dr. visit co-pays but then nothing that was done in the office was covered. She has a thyroid issue and sees her Dr. 3x per year. They are moving towards possible removal of her thyroid altogether. She''s trying to avoid that but it''s going in that direction. We put her income at $43,463 giving her a $783 ATPC for 2025. She wants Dr. Claudia Panzer. I looked her up and she doesn''t show up in any network. I looked up the dr. site and it says they accept all insurance.  I told her to call and verfiy directly with the Drs. office as well. DOB 5/12/62 and 80012. She chose the Cigna Connect CO Option Gold.  Her cost is $175.81.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-11 15:50:21', '2024-11-11 15:51:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151643018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069438001', 'Beth Blacker', NULL, '11-11-24 Beth thinks she will be earning less next year bc of the election results. She sees the habits of her clients treat her services as more of a luxury than necessity.  She thinks she will earn  around $38,740 and gets a $782.03 APTC for 2025.  Her cost is $316.18. Last years she reported $61,740. So, after reviewing the plans her current Cigna Connect Flex Gold $950 is only $2 more than the same plan at $2700 ded. She might need a foot surgery. She''s been happy with her current plan. It''s all set for 2025. I told her to call Cigna just to make sure her plan is set with auto pay into 2025.

