  ('zcrm_1579374000151393116', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, '11-8-24 From Cami re Susie, Hey Wendy,

 

Before our call, here is some background info on Spondyloarthritis, all are quick reads:

https://spondylitis.org/about-spondylitis/overview-of-spondyloarthritis/
https://www.womenshealthmag.com/health/a46887502/everything-you-need-to-know-about-axial-spondyloarthritis/
https://www.womenshealthmag.com/health/a46860028/how-to-assemble-a-care-team-for-axial-spondyloarthritis/
 

Preliminarily, her Dr. believes that she has Axial & Peripheral Spondyloarthritis, not Ankylosing. Her doctor is recommending that she start Biologic treatment ASAP, but we will wait until we get the official diagnosis from Dr. Zell (Rheumatologist), who Susie is seeing on November 19th.

 

Here are a few other items that she has been diagnosed with that previous doctors treated but did not string together until she started seeing Dr. Silver, just a few weeks back:

 

Iritis/Uveitis – started in her 20’s, brought on by severe stress
Arthritis in her big toe – 2019
Burning pain in her ankle – 2023
Low Back, Hip Pain & overall stiffness – this was how the doctor put it all together – never treated or diagnosed but has had pain since she was a kid
 

Talking with her doctor and reading through the Women’s Health link above, all of these things are clearly connected, but it took Dr. Silver to string all the pieces together. While the diagnosis is scary, it’s also empowering for Susie to finally have answers and support.

 

My biggest concern with Zion is that this is a genetic disorder, and it will be a lifetime of management for Susie. It’s directly related to Susie''s blood marker, HLA-B27. In 2017 she had a doctor refer her to a Rheumatologist to get scans of her SI joint to look for signs of MS, which is a potential factor of HLA B27. At that time, neither MS nor Spondyloarthritis was determined by the referring doctor. Neither of us can remember who made that referral or why.

 

In the case of my neck, Zion has called my degenerative disc disease ‘pre-existing’ because it is genetic. I fear they will take that stance with Sus as well. So, while in the short term, there should be enough $$ there to get Susie started on treatments and into remission, long-term Zion may not be the best option for either of us.

 

Looking forward to talking with you and getting your perspective & as always, thank you so much for your time & support.

 

Cami"

They are in their 4th year of membership, so they will get up to $125K per incident, per rolling 12 months and it resets every year. So, they think they will never reach the $125K for these items. They will also meet the 3 Needs per year. They already have 3 and now adding to it. They realize they are better off with MCS and Zion rather than moving to reg. ins. at this point. They will go ahead and create 2 new needs one for above and other for lump in breast.  They also Love HAB. They Love Dr. Silver who is a Functional Medicine Dr. in Boulder who figured out what''s wrong with Susie when nobody else could figure out all of the pieces.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-08 13:24:39', '2024-11-08 13:24:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151392231', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000149300002', 'Angela Rank', NULL, '11/8/24: Angie called to reschedule welcome call for 13th. She already set it up online. Let her know she is good to go and we will reach out on that day. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-08 13:08:57', '2024-11-08 13:08:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151393111', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045438013', 'Drew Cifrodelli', NULL, '11-8-24 Drew is interested in dropping Redirect and adding HAB. He had a terrible experience with getting a full lab panel covered by anyone. Lab Corp basically billed Medicaid, then US Health erroneously first. Then they finally billed Redirect. Redirect covered their portion and Lab Corp barely dropped the price and kept the bill at thousands of dollars. They wouldn''t give him the cash price bc they billed these other entities. He has finally paid off the bill after they sent it to collections. So brutal!  He''s wide awake to all of the corruption in the healthcare world and beyond. Chose to run for Sheriff as part of his way to help enlighten fellow people and keep everyone safe. He got the shingles shot at some point in the past which gave him neuropathy! 
He thought that his kids were on his membership but it doesn''t show that on our end. However, he received a new Redirect Health card on Oct. 10th and it shows Cole and Dylan, twins, on his card!  He thought he added them but they change it every year due to shared responsibility with his x. Fortunately he believes the kids are currently on his x''s plan with trad ins. So, he won''t worry about them for now. He will use dental, vision, possibly nutritionist since he has an allergy to gluten and would love help, etc.
We might be able to move him to CARE+ $350 and HAB $107 = $457,   This is much cheaper than $607 if he stays put, since he can''t move to Premium Care bc he''s already a member. UGH!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-08 12:48:00', '2024-11-12 10:23:29'),
