  ('zcrm_1579374000151181031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091116', 'Gregory Vassie', NULL, 'No response. Left a detailed message on vm. Sent email to reschedule the welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-07 09:02:28', '2024-11-07 09:02:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151181016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125085043', 'Myles Vlachos', NULL, 'No response. Mailbox full. Not able to leave message. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-07 08:32:26', '2024-11-07 08:32:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151181008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125287001', 'Deena Patel', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Put in request to Kelly to resend out QR life code card to member. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-07 07:46:11', '2024-11-07 07:58:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151075231', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169157001', 'Shawn Aycock', NULL, '11-6-24 Shawn is 58, 1-21-66 and partner Lisa is 4-13-64. They live in 80015. Came to me via Andrea as a new client. Shawn is not working other than part time 1099 for about $40K. Lisa is looking to quit her job with benefits and they aren''t sure what her income will be. They will be living off investments. For wellness they do screenings, dental, vision, skin sometimes, mammo, colonoscopies, gym, but no mental health or nutrition bc don''t need it. I quoted her plans on C4 which were crazy expensive without APTC. They''ll have to figure out their income. Then I quoted Premium Care $1000/$575 + HAB $200 = $775 plus $125/$25. She''s very interested in this but wants to share it with Lisa and absorb it all.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-06 23:07:13', '2024-11-06 23:07:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151075226', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063253037', 'Bobbi Georgeton', NULL, '11-6-24 Bobbi is deciding between an HSA plan or the RMHP $0 Ded for about a $30 savings but higher MOP.  Chris looks like he should keep his plan. If they do so, their cost will be nearly identical to last year with their income at $180K, I think.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-06 23:00:00', '2024-11-06 23:00:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151075221', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171447', 'Dorian Merrill', NULL, '11-6-24 I sent this to Dorian, "It looks like you''re paying $299 right now. We could make the switch and remove the new ARM wellness insurance benefit and replace it with Health Access. If you choose to do so, the new monthly contribution will be $354.15.&nbsp;  Let me know if you want to talk further."
It''s $232.15 SDHC+$15 Sedera''s Fee+HAB $107= $354.15.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-06 22:32:57', '2024-11-06 22:32:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000151075216', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082413134', 'Nathan Knecht', NULL, '11-6-24 Hi Wendy,

I would like to review some option with you when you have a chance, I’m available at your earliest convenience.  Our Cigna plan will auto renew and our premium is going up $100 from $575 to $675.  I’ve liked Cigna so maybe we have a plan 1 tier down?  We would also be curious about additional benefits.

Nathan

My response - 
Nice to hear from you. The options below what you have a pretty terrible. They don''t cover anything until you spend the full deductible amount. I''d say, if you''re happy with your current plan, then I''d keep it. 

I also shared HAB info.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-06 21:15:41', '2024-11-06 21:15:41'),
