  ('zcrm_1579374000150898016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000088688010', 'Caroline Jackson', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 08:19:26', '2024-11-05 08:19:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150888024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141685002', 'Laura Murtha', NULL, '11.05.2024 Zack called to learn what his next steps are in the NOW deemed shareable medical need with Zion. They requested via email to for him to fulfill his $1000 IUA. He said he''s already paid $6000. I led him to open his sharing request in zion''s member portal, he did, and he found where and HOW to upload his itemized statements and receipts. It was nice to share for the first time that members can actually fulfill their IUA straight through their member portal with Zion now. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 08:03:03', '2024-11-05 08:03:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150902003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000078939464', 'Krista Irmischer', NULL, '11/5
Krista called she has been diagnosed with cancer and needs more info on how to navigate this situation.A&gt;C', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 07:37:55', '2024-11-05 07:37:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150888008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000114056002', 'David Mell', NULL, '11.05.2024 Dave called wondering how to maneuver his financial responsibility and benefits, with going to see urgent care or ER, due to a head injury he sustained. He questioned why I recommended to present as cash pay vs just presenting his insurance card, ARM. 
I pulled up his profile and led him through the difference between the high deductible on his card vs the IUA of $1000. He was receptive and ready to present in that lens instead. I touched on collecting paperwork to upload onto the medical need as well as the 6 month deadline. Dave will call us back when he is ready to open that medical need with Zion. 
Dave also needs to change his address, so I sent him the MPB Change form via CRM. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 07:35:54', '2024-11-05 07:36:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150898008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125085043', 'Myles Vlachos', NULL, 'No response. Mailbox full. Not able to leave a message on vm. Sent email to reschedule welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 07:32:46', '2024-11-05 07:32:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150888003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145346174', 'Scott Garcia', NULL, '11.05.2024 Susan called on behalf of her husband Scott, regarding a shoulder injury he sustained over the weekend. They had called an ortho who was willing to see them on Monday, for a consultation fee of $1000. They found that to be an absurd fee, so they started shopping around for a better amount. They live in the mountains where specialists or medical services are scarce. There is a hospital that they might be able to get in, and they are planning to connect with them today to learn more of what their options are. 
If/when they get in today, they will present as cash pay, collect their paperwork, and call us back with their next steps adhered by their specialist. That will be whether they need surgery, PT, MRI or all. 
***************************************************************
none until next week
no mri till he sees a physician

considering to go to the initial doctor $1000 ....

Sedera 3-way with Thomas
freedom to see whoever
fulfill the $1000 IUA before community of funds  
after submitting bills - medical description needed - 4-6 weeks to get reimbursed unless cost is so inflated then negotiations take place, and that takes around 3-4 months. Sedera will negotiate.
  pay as little as possible so there''s a larger leverage to negotiate. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-05 07:19:59', '2024-11-05 08:39:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150771094', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000171503002', 'Resa Hayes', NULL, '11-4-24 Resa is 53 and lost her husband to esophageal cancer 3 years ago, 2021. She has 3 adult kids but 2 on her ins now. One is turning 19 next week and he is going to college in CA. Her daughter is 25 soon and in school in NY. Since they both may need to show proof of ACA compliant ins, I quoted her Secure HSA. Also since one is in CA, Secure is the only option for CA. However, they all still claim residency in CO for now. When her husband was getting treated for cancer they chose to get treated out of state which meant they paid $3500 for a plan flexible enough to allow for out of state services. I also shared HAB bc she''s a psychotherapist and her clients keep telling her about their membership with HAB. She''s very interested in that as well for the mental health benefits, etc.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-04 23:08:23', '2024-11-11 20:33:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150771089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081634027', 'Julia Bolz', NULL, '11-4-24 Julia wants to determine what''s best moving forward. She was frustrated by her recent experiences with various aspects of the membership. She has VSP Choice Plan A at $15.97 and got coverage of $129 for glasses. She was expecting a bigger reimbursement. She went through Costco online for some items and they are apparently separate from the physical Costco locations. So, that is frustrating. She had an eye appt for $356! She has prescription sunglasses and contacts also. I sent her the brochure to read through to see if she''s owed anything for those. 
She also fell down the stairs in Oct which created a back and ankle injury. The chiro discovered degenerative back issues and they are separating it into 2 needs. She''s paid $1907 already. Separating it will mean no sharing she thinks. 
She also has a dermatology issue recently which was $1004 and she was reimbursed $4. 
She also may need help with a bursitis issue. If she winds up having 3 Needs starting after Sept. 1st, she could get the 3rd need shared by HAB.
Finally she has compounded meds for hormones but that''s never shared by ins or mcs. 
She''s paying for Delta Dental and that''s been good bc  it paid for all but about $15 per dental cleaning. It sounds like she does 3 per year possibly. She''s unsure if she should keep HAB since she just did many of her wellness visits already in 2024.   She may want to talk further.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-04 22:56:27', '2024-11-04 22:56:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150771084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000150922026', 'Colton Arnold', NULL, '11-4-24 Colton came via Shawna Sands. He lives in TX. He has a baby coming soon who is due Dec. 27th. His wife is all set. But, he wants to put the baby onto his plan upon birth, so in essence Jan. 1st. He will watch the video and we will connect tomorrow morning.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-04 22:47:30', '2024-11-05 09:00:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150771079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000150772245', 'Kelleigh Condon', NULL, '11-4-24 Kelleigh is working with a broker already on C4 but was curious about MCS. She''s wisely deciding to stay with C4 for now. Very nice and thankful for my help.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-11-04 22:04:59', '2024-11-04 22:04:59'),
