  ('zcrm_1579374000150692003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000087734002', 'Jocelyn Luhr', NULL, '10.31.24:  Jocelyn texted me apologizing for the delay in responding. I asked if she heard my phone message notifying her that if she intends to cancel her plan she needs to do it by today. She asked me to email her the other options I mentioned and she would take a look at them and get back to me by 4 p.m. She said her partner has stage 4 cancer and it''s not going well and she has 3 children she''s juggling. Sounds like price is a major issue at this point for her.
I emailed her the best options for her (Premium Care and Direct) and described them w/pricing for each.
She emailed me back the following:
 
"For now I want to stay with Zion. The catch is that I pay a DPC doctor right now as it is, so I’m going to just switch back to Zion in December. I just need to ensure that my account remains consistent because of issues that Zion has paid for and are recurring and I need it to stay that way.
Thank you for your persistence & help on this."

I emailed her back to ask what Zion plan she is taking, Direct or Essential (I told her that the 2025 price for her for this plan would be $194/mo. w/ a $1000 IUA but she gets no other services except MCS). And I asked if Zion referred her DPC physician to her. (*Note:  I''m considering that Zion may have convinced her it would be less costly if she cancels her MPB plan and enrolls with a DPC and Zion directly).

I also advised her that she has to be sure she pays her share fee for 11/1 to continue her membership through November so she doesn''t lose her Zion membership status. She has received 2 notices from Patti informing her that her payment was declined due to insufficient funds. Waiting to hear back from her.', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-11-01 10:48:14', '2024-11-01 10:54:23'),
