  ('zcrm_1579374000150316118', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130373002', 'Lisa Wiesen', NULL, '10-29-24 Lisa wants to remove her husband Kurt for Jan. 1st bc of Medicare age and add HAB for herself for Jan. 1st effective.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 21:33:56', '2024-10-29 21:33:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150316108', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000150772245', 'Kelleigh Condon', NULL, '10-29-24 Kelleigh is 63 and referred by Kallie Carpenter. Kelleigh lives in Carbondale, CO which is Garfield County, 81623. She had a hip replacement 2 years ago as of March 2025. She had complications when she skied. The hip was possibly too loose, so they gave her injections to try to grow the bone. The last visit with a Revision Specialist was in April of 2024. She also has cold/infection induced asthma and osteopenia. She doesn''t qualify for America''s Choice, she won''t qualify for a subsidy bc of an inheritance due to her mom passing away and MPB is a bit risky.  She takes estazolam and escitalopram. She needs to start Jan. 1st. ACA plans look to be $1000-$1400 for EO. The only way MCS could work is if she saved the $800 x12 savings which is $9600 to use towards any smaller medical needs, then she''d be ahead. But, if something bad happens with any pre-x, it''s not good.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 20:42:46', '2024-10-29 20:42:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150300256', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000105471002', 'Keri Henry', NULL, '10/29/24: Keri sent the following email:
I am reaching out to see if I can get a consolidation of my statements/payments starting in January 2023-current. I need them for legal purposes and all I have are emailed invoice information, nothing downloadable, but just the email itself. I need something that states what was owed and what was paid monthly, are you able to help me out with this so I don’t have to print off 1.5 years worth of emails.
I also tried to login in to the website to get this information and was never emailed with a link to update my password and am unable to access my account.

Responded with instructions on how to access her statements inside member portal and provided log in credentials from CRM  (which worked fine when testing).AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 17:38:52', '2024-10-29 17:38:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150300251', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109789017', 'Pamela Wende', NULL, '10/29/24: Pamela called with questions about vendor change and aging into Medicare. I confirmed that she didn''t need to do anything about the vendor change and explained what that would look like from her end. We also discussed MCS, Cirrus, MEC. I advised her to speak to Leslie about her specific questions related to Medicare but informed her that she would age out of this plan at 65. Suggested she give us a call before any future appts so we can guide her on how best to use her plan. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 17:16:58', '2024-10-29 17:16:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150300246', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130562001', 'Philip Ender', NULL, '10/29/24: Esther called inquiring if her plan includes orthodontics. I informed her that unfortunately no. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 17:14:54', '2024-10-29 17:14:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150300241', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000146503026', 'William Skabelund', NULL, '10/29/24: Sarah called, irritated at first because she stated no one has gotten back to her or been able to provide her the information she needs for ARM card. While on the phone I provided her contact info and the group number - as well as helping her access her member portal. 
Saw that Acelyn sent their cards earlier today. Forwarded another copy and called to make sure member received the card. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 17:11:03', '2024-10-29 17:11:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150316103', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130373002', 'Lisa Wiesen', NULL, '10-29-24 From Lisa, "Thanks for sending me this information. After reviewing both options I''ve decided that I want to add the Wellness benefit to my current plan (I think that''s Secure Health?). It''s the plan with a monthly cost of $459. As I recall, this provides me with better flexibility for alternative care doctors and I won''t have to worry about the three-year pre-existing conditions clause with Sedera. 

Please let me know if I have this information correct and what I need to do next. Thanks so much for your help! "', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 16:57:33', '2024-10-29 16:57:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150316085', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061924134', 'Kristen Lassalette', NULL, '10-29-24 Kristen is choosing to drop MEC and add HAB. She needs a follow up ultrasound to a mammo for wellness. Aspen Valley Medical was going to charge her $900 with Planstin since not ACA compliant. She cancelled her appt and called me for solutions. She''s now enrolled for Dec. 1st to handle that and a skin check (I think she said) in Jan. She might choose to keep this once she ages in Medicare. She will use many of these benefits ongoing.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 15:58:58', '2024-10-29 16:04:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150300203', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000091225002', 'Robert Howell', NULL, '10/29/24: Gimena called requesting to update address. Emailed form to do so to her personal email: gimenahowell@gmail.com. AM', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 15:38:27', '2024-10-29 15:38:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150316075', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000150571023', 'Robert Reese', NULL, '10-29-24 Bob is 57 and an ASHI member. His wife is 52 but gets ins through her employer and only has to pay $90. If they add him it''s close to $500. He''s healthy. His only issue is slighly elevated cholesterol and blood sugar, but never any meds for either. He had a colonoscopy around age 50, so probably 3 more years until he needs one.  He doesn''t really want the immunizations. He got the shingles shot and was in bed for 4 days following it. He''s interested in Premium care $1000/$285 + HAB $107 = $392 or $1500/$254 +$107 = $361 and $125/$25 - $100 for ASHI member. He''s also inquiring for his daughter in law but she''s pregnant already. So, she will have to wait. I priced out Care+ and Premium Care and described the differences She may want to join next year for her and the kids. Her husband/Bob''s son is on the same employer plan as his wife which is really good for the employee, just not for family members. So, he''s all set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 15:04:15', '2024-10-29 15:04:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150338093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000069994449', 'Leah Houston', NULL, '10.29.2024 Leah called saying that she''s paid in full for the last 2 years and has not received any correspondence from us.
After searching for her in Admin123, I learned that she indeed has been cancelled, and due to non payment, according to accounting/Karina Garcia. 
I did not have a whole of direct answers for Leah so I was able to get a hold of Karina, and she asked me to transfer her to her. NT', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2024-10-29 14:52:22', '2024-10-29 14:54:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000150316064', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993160', 'Karen Peirson', NULL, '10-29-24 Ursula called and cancelled the duplicate Co-Op membership that was showing at $1020 and was enrolled on 10-8-24 at 10:21 pm. We have no idea how that happened. They didn''t enroll in that. They are all set with proper billing now for $315 only for HAB.

"As discussed, we had 2 memberships for her and her family. 

- Health Access Preventive Any DPC - Effective 10/1/24 (Received 8/28/24)
- Health Access Preventive + Coop $1000 with Any DPC - Effective 11/1/24 (Received on 10/8/24)

I have cancelled the duplicate membership with the Coop plan and only left active the Health Access Preventive for $315 per month."

They are all set with just preventive through Health Access.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-29 14:50:41', '2024-10-29 14:55:15'),
