  ('zcrm_1579374000149765061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171242', 'Paige Cox', NULL, '10.23.2024 Paige left a VM on where to go to get a biopsy. I got her VM much later, so I will call her first thing tomorrow morning. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-23 17:57:24', '2024-10-23 17:57:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149765056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000141096012', 'Matt Eytcheson', NULL, '10.23.2024 Matt''s VM was left in the system, so I called him back. He said he was taken care of by another one of our team members. He will call us if he has any questions, trying to open his sharing request via Zion''s member portal. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-23 17:55:11', '2024-10-23 17:55:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149765051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601108', 'Kevin Fechtmeyer', NULL, '10.23.2024 Sarah called to initially learn how to search for providers, and the conversation slowly branched out to learning the entire membership, parts of the essential services and how to get covered for hormone therapy.
I broke down her membership in three parts: Essentials, Preventive and Health Sharing.
I offered the main parts to the Essential services: CirrusMD, Fullscript and M&S EAP.
We went over preventive resources: Multiplan, Labs & Healthcare.GOV.
We went over healthsharing medical needs with Sedera - we did a 3-way call with Sedera and spoke with Chris, who shares that Kevin and Sarah DO NOT show up as members in their database.
We talked about getting that medical need for her hormone therapy started with Sedera, so they can determine it eligible or not.
She will seek a licensed medical professional for those services, keep all her receipts, observe her IUA and maintain reciprocation with Sedera''s medical need specialists.
I put in a ticket with IT to make sure that their file is integrated properly with Sedera.
I sent her emails on Preventive Resources and Lab Resources. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-23 17:30:24', '2024-10-23 17:30:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149749128', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153173005', 'Peter Ernst', NULL, '10-23-24 Diane is 35 and husband is 34 with 2 kids under 2. Diane does contract work and her husband is  doesn''t get ins through his employer. They came to me via Maggie Tolan. They are healthy and primarily focus on wellness visits for kids and need to update themselves for adult well checks. She watched the video. She had leukemia over 10 years ago and it''s been gone ever since, no meds or anything. No pre-x. They do dental cleanings, ski pass and yoga for gym, skin checks maybe in future, mental health yes, labs, yes, vax for kids, not adults. Only Zoloft for meds for Diane and nobody else. They moved from FC to Carbondale recently and need to reestablish with new drs.  Quoted CARE+ EF $672 and HAB EF $250 = $922. They are looking for a Dec. 1st effective date. We have our next appt on Monday of next week.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-23 16:30:23', '2024-10-23 16:30:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149765046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120991001', 'Suchada Chaiwechakarn', NULL, '10.23.2024 Suchada called to confirm she can get her flu and covid shot at the pharmacy and get covered. We recently have been guided that members need to go to their physicians/annual physical to get their vaccines, b/c of how pharmacies bill, through the prescription program and the not the insurance. It does not get covered that way.
Suchada was adamant that she would be covered via pharmacy, given her past experience. IDK when the change took place, and I was hoping the 3 way call with Planstin would provide that shift. We, Caitlyn and I, reiterated the imperativeness of going to the Dr or taking a gamble and to going to the pharmacy, and directing them to bill the insurance not the scripts program. NT', 'Nahla Tebcherany', 'Nahla Tebcherany', '2024-10-23 15:52:16', '2024-10-23 15:52:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149749123', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000156429012', 'Amy Beley', NULL, '10-23-24 Amy, 45 was referred by Stephanie Yost. Amy lives in La Platta County, zip 81301. She expects to earn $220K. She''s planning to leave her company that she''s working for and venture out on her own. She expects same pay as with her employer. She wants a more flexible work life. She has a young son. She watched the video. No tobacco and meds for asthma and allergy to yellow jacket bees. She understands the pre-x clause. She hasn''t been hospitalized for asthma since she was a young kid. She will likely use ALL categories of HAB and she prefers alternative drs, chiro, acu, etc. CARE+ EC $461 + HAB $200 = $661. I forgot to mention the $125/$25. I''ll add that to an email. She''s also interested in dental discount plan and vision. She thinks her son might need ortho some day as well.  For asthma and allergies she takes monolukast, Symbicort and one other we looked up. They were all cheaper or close to her co-pay that she pays now. DOB is 6/16/79 and son is 6/17/21.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-23 15:51:47', '2025-01-06 17:07:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149749106', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002095005', 'Dustin Spencer', NULL, '10-23-24 October 23, 2024 at 12:26 PM

Dear Dustin Tracy Spencer,

Username: du**************************

To help you sign into your account, we provided a username hint above, but cannot display your full username due to security reasons.

Important: Renew your health and/or dental plan through Connect for Health Colorado® for 2025

Your health and/or dental insurance plan is ready for renewal. Your current plan will be offered in 2025, with the name Cigna Connect Colorado Option Silver. We estimate your 2025 advance premium tax credit will be $388.96 which will lower your new monthly premium to $36.03, starting January 1, 2025.

You can view your renewal options in your account from November 1, 2024 through December 1, 2024. Starting November 1st, review and update your information to make sure you are accessing all the savings that you qualify for.

After December 1, 2024, we will automatically renew you in your current plan(s), and the insurance company will bill you for the January 2025 premium, unless one of the following occurs: you select a different plan, you cancel the renewal plan(s), or your 2024 plan ends before December 31, 2024. Your 2024 enrollment(s) must stay effective until December 31, 2024, for you to automatically renew in your current plan(s).

By December 1, 2024:

Step 1: Sign into your account at ConnectforHealthCO.com, or contact your certified Broker or Assister, starting November 1, 2024.

Step 2: Review your account and application information such as address, household size and income, and make updates as needed. If updates are not needed, proceed to Step 3

Step 3: Select “Start My Renewal”. You’ll be able to review your application information and the renewal plans. You can review the benefits and determine whether your needs will be met by the renewing plan(s); the benefits may be different including covered doctors, prescriptions and costs.

Federal law requires that we compare the information on your application with other data sources. If your information does not match those data sources, we’ll ask you to provide more information. Don’t worry, this will be easy to do!

Step 4: If your plan meets your budget and health needs, renew your current plan(s) on your Review Renewal Plans page. If you do not take action by December 1, 2024 and your plan(s) is still active, your plan(s) will automatically renew.

You can also review other plan options and select a different plan that meets your budget and health needs or stop the automatic renewal by opting out of your renewal plan(s) for 2025.

Step 5: Contact your insurance company to confirm your January payment and ongoing payment method, including any auto-draft payments, by December 20, 2024.

Estimated Monthly Costs in 2025:

Your Estimated Monthly Premium Tax Credit for 2025:

Your Estimated Monthly Premium for 2025 with the Premium Tax Credit:

Your Monthly Premium without Premium Tax Credit for 2025:

$388.96	$36.03	$424.99
Your Current Monthly Premium Tax Credit:

Your Current Monthly Premium with the Premium Tax Credit:

Your Current Monthly Premium without Premium Tax Credit:

$386.60	$0.00	$386.60
We estimated the amount of premium tax credit you qualify for in 2025 based on your latest application. (If you made changes to your application after the date of this letter, the estimated premium tax credit may not accurately reflect what you qualify for now.) It is your responsibility to review and update your application if needed, so we can accurately determine what kind of and how much financial help you can receive for the rest of 2024 and in 2025. You will be required to file a federal tax return for every year that you receive tax credits. You’ll need to reconcile what you received with the IRS based on the income shown on your federal income tax return. If you don’t file federal taxes correctly for two years in a row in which you get premium tax credits, you may no longer qualify for a tax credit in the future.

The Open Enrollment Period for 2025 is from November 1, 2024 to January 15, 2025. Once you pay your premium for January 2025, you cannot change plans outside of the Open Enrollment Period, unless you experience a Qualified Life Change Event. Report any changes to your household size and income within sixty (60) days of the change.

Questions about your plan benefits?

Call or visit the insurance company’s website to confirm your providers and prescriptions are covered by the new plan. Please note providers can frequently change plans and insurance companies. The insurance companies have the most up-to-date lists of providers they cover.

For plan or benefit questions, please call Cigna at 1-877-900-1237 Monday through Friday, 8:00a.m. to 10:00p.m. EST and 9:00a.m. to 5:00p.m. EST on Saturdays or visit http://www.Cigna.com.

Thank you for renewing your coverage with us.

Sincerely,
Connect for Health Colorado®', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-23 15:36:50', '2024-10-23 15:36:50'),
