  ('zcrm_1579374000149488003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000145560002', 'Stephanie Thompson', NULL, '10-21-24 Dr. Helen Rho PCP, Dr. Heather Bright Hoffmeyer Obgyn. Appt next week with Dr. Rho.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-21 15:22:20', '2024-10-21 15:37:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149430018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000140549002', 'Patricia Nilsen', NULL, '10-21-24 I called patty back and the flu shot is included in her Health Access membership. I explained to her how to submit for reimbursement. She was happy to hear it and will move forward to do so. All set.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-21 14:54:13', '2024-10-21 14:54:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149430013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000138597002', 'Bladimir Aviles', NULL, '10-21-24 I called Bladimir back bc he wanted to find out if his clinic was in network. Then he wanted to cancel. He has a new health issue that he went to the ER in Aug. He has a $5K bill that he''s freaking out about and had already enrolled in Mass Health without an APTC. I asked him if he submitted the Need and he said yes. But, then he later told me he hasn''t paid his $1000 yet. I''m not sure that he created a Need. He was SO, SO confused.  I explained it to him 3 more times. He confirmed that his issue is brand new and nothing will be on his record before his June 1st start date. He said he went to the ER for a stomach issue and they can''t find any problems. Then he got a $5K bill. He didn''t want to have to pay for more visits. I let him know as long as it''s not pre-x which he confirmed then once he pays his $1000 the cost above that will be paid according to the sharing guidelines. I let him know nothing will be paid until he pays his portion which is $1000.  If he swtiches to Mass Health, he''ll have to pay his $750 ded and $1000 mop again. So, he''s going to lose by doing so. I gave him the Concierge phone number and told him to start there. He will cancel Mass Health. I let him know there''s no network. I also let him know if he goes back to the ER for this same health issue, it will cost him $500. So, if he can use Urgent Care then it won''t cost him more above his IUA assuming it''s all part of the same health issue and according the guidelines.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-21 14:45:36', '2024-10-21 14:45:36'),
