  ('zcrm_1579374000149168036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142598002', 'Heather Bingaman', NULL, '10-17-24 Heather was overwhelmed and wanted to cancel bc she hasn''t seen the value. So, I went through everything with her that she needs to do moving forward. She has 3 dental cleanings, 1 for each kid, 1 wellness visit for herself. She can be reimbursed for all of that totaling around $1000 right away. Her daughter broke her wrist last day of school but long before enrolling. She doesn''t have any new expenses for that Aug. onward. She got rear ended on Aug. 21st and so far has only paid $94 for a visit but may need PT and chiro for whiplash and a concussion. I told her to create a new need in case the costs ever exceed her $1000 IUA. I let her know that car insurance will be the primary in this case and MCS secondary. But, it''s still beneficial to create a new need, just in case the expenses exceed $1000 down the road. I''ll send her instructions for each.  They also just bought a new house, started a new job and dealing with so much that she was super overwhelmed. But, she keeps the records of everything so that''s not a problem.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-17 15:50:10', '2024-10-17 15:51:18'),
