  ('zcrm_1579374000149168026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104457002', 'Normandie Rainwater', NULL, '10-17-24 They might move to VT! She can keep her current membership and show proof of MEC if necessary. But, according to MPB''s document, VT does not have a penalty for non compliance at this point.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-17 15:22:41', '2024-10-17 15:22:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149144013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000144870002', 'Aubrey Winik', NULL, '10/17/24
Aubrey called because he needed his arm card and wanted to know if Ozempic would be covered, I informed him that it would not. the only meds covered at 100% are statin.', 'Acelyn Calderon', 'Acelyn Calderon', '2024-10-17 15:19:21', '2024-10-17 15:19:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149168021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000149171001', 'Damrong Trairatnobhas', NULL, '10-17-24 Damrong is Laura''s husband. Laura aged into Medicare from Big-E Commerce/Corbel Universe''s group plan direct to Sedera since Dec. 2018. Dave Abajian is able to keep his plan intact as a solo member of the group. Laura is cancelling her membership for Oct. 31st. Damrong is joining MPB''s Premium Care membership now that he''s on his own without Laura. I will request his original start date once I have Laura''s cancellation form.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-17 15:14:28', '2024-10-17 15:14:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149148163', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000081634027', 'Julia Bolz', NULL, '10/17/24: Julia called with 3 questions:
1. She recently fell down the stairs and has paid over $2000 towards the incident. Is this a new sharing request issue. I explained yes, and that she would be responsible for another IUA. 
Educated member on the difference between IUA and Deductible. 
Doctor is suggesting stem cell treatment for her hip > is this shareable? Zion would have to tell her for certain, but it could possibly be categorized as a therapeutic treatment. 
2. She recently went to eye doctor and paid for exam, glasses and contacts. Is this part of wellness benefit? While it''s not part of her MEC benefit, I do see that member has a vision benefit and health access. I explained that those are different from MPB plan, provided phone number from notes and said she could also reach out to Wendy about those benefits. 
3. Interested in Bio-Identical hormone therapy. Is this shareable? According to Zion guiedelines, Hormone injections are but there is a cap to how much Zion will share. But to get a definite answer, I can connect her with Zion.
Ended by transferring to Zion to gain clarity on stem cell treatment and hormone treatment. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-17 15:14:09', '2024-10-17 15:14:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149154018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000129828002', 'Emma Donovan', NULL, 'Emma submitted the Cognito form requesting the change for 12-1-2024.  Spoke with Patti, we cannot do it for 12-1.  We CAN do it for 11-1 or 1-1 only.  Told her I found out we are in the midst of a system-wide update and we''re locked out of making the change for 12-1. Emma called me back a few minutes later and has chosen to go with 11-1. I told her to reply to my email indicating 11/1 since the Cognito form said 12-1. Emma said she will send the email. I told Patti to change the Cognito form to 11-1. I will put Emma''s email in here as soon as I see it.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-10-17 15:09:43', '2024-10-17 15:09:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149154013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000058609028', 'Teresa Smith', NULL, '10-17-2026  Terri wants to make herself the primary.  But to do that we will need to cancel her and have her re-enroll at the same time.  I called her and told her the best way to do this is in January of 2025 as we cannot do it now due to system changes, MEC upgrade to ARM behind the scenes and new pricing for 2025.  She is concerned about double charges; told here there would be none and that I will walk her through the cancel and re-enroll all on one phone call in January.  I will contact her in the 2nd week of Jan 2025 to make this happen.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2024-10-17 14:46:51', '2024-10-17 14:46:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149148123', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000093922012', 'Jennifer Letz', NULL, '10/17/24: Jennifer called wondering when she was going to receive the discounts for her rsv and flu shots? From our records she was emailed coupons yesterday. Member was able to locate the email in her spam folder. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-17 14:19:27', '2024-10-17 14:19:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149148114', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000120264002', 'Cheryl Powell', NULL, '10/17/24: Cheryl called wanting to reset her sessions with EAP and wondering if that was different since she changed her plan. I explained that it is the same for all MPB plans, and M&amp;SEAP handles all tracking of sessions with them. Cheryl said she would wmail Sherry. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-17 14:06:00', '2024-10-17 14:06:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149167043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779589', 'Jennifer Anderson', 'New Enrollment eff 11/24', 'Member Only $1000 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-10-17 13:58:27', '2024-10-17 13:58:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149167038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779589', 'Jennifer Anderson', NULL, 'This Member was a previous Sedera member then did the conversion to Zion in 8/20.  She then stayed on Membership until she got Employer benefits eff 1/22.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2024-10-17 13:57:33', '2024-10-17 13:57:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000149148109', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000109799008', 'Reginald Ashby', NULL, '10/17/24: Reginald called to see how much he''s paid into his plan for the year 2023. I informed him that he can always look up this information through his member portal, but since he wan''t near a computer - I calculated how much he''s paid MPB which was 4,882.20 for the year 2023. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-17 13:51:10', '2024-10-17 13:51:10');
