  ('zcrm_1579374000149148008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000111775010', 'Xiaosong Xiao', NULL, '10/17/24: Member emailed me wondering why he only received a $153.99 reimbursement for his bills. I explained what Danielle from Zion told me about his sharing request: 
Zion was unable to share in the preventive services like vaccines and other items listed as preventive. Additionally, they were unable to share in the prescription because the name of the medication wasn’t included in the documents you provided. However, they are willing to assist with the medication if it''s related to the same issue, member would just need to provide documentation with the prescription name.
Additionally, I called Planstin to check on the reimbursement he submitted and learned the following:
Karen informed me that they emailed Xiaosong on October 1st requesting the CPT codes for the Park Nicollet visit. Essentially, they need a "superbill" with the medical codes in order to process the claim.

Advised Member that in order to have more of his bills reimbursed, he would need to provide the right documentation. Zion requires the names of all services and treatments, and Planstin requires the CPT codes - a superbill -  for services. AM', 'Angee Montgomery', 'Angee Montgomery', '2024-10-17 08:28:05', '2024-10-17 08:28:05'),
