  ('zcrm_1579374000149011013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124672026', 'Jessica Bartmann', NULL, '10-16-24 Sean Burke helped me cancel plan on IC Quotes with termination date 10-31-24 and generated Cobra letter and sent it to Jessica and Jennifer Abbott. Now I''m on hold with Cigna to cancel her plan and the auto pay. They don''t have a way to do cancellations without calling Cigan for Brokers. Hector is working on the paperwork to complete the process while I''m on hold.
Jessica has not been to the dr. in 2024 and hasn''t used any of her deductible. So, we can cancel her current plan through employer/ICHRA and start with the same plan newly via C4HCO and get her a subsidy. She''s starting 1099 work in Nov and Dec. She''s trying to figure out her best guess as to her income for just starting out those 2 months. She will likely get a significant APTC at first. Then as she gets going next year, she''s thinking she''ll earn $80K-$90K.
Hector with Cigna completed the cancellation on his end and cancelled the auto pay. Her plan ID is 98A57N. Termination is effective Oct. 31st, 2024. It will be processed in 2-3 business days. A letter will be sent to Jessica within 7 days. I will see it in the Broker Portal the last week of Oct. The confirmation # is 569125. All set for cancellation.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2024-10-16 12:32:43', '2024-10-16 12:40:50'),
