  ('zcrm_1579374000148911003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000107134002', 'Thomas Beaudin', NULL, '10.15.24:  Recvd. an email response from Thomas, he is available to meet today. I confirmed with him.
Called Thomas - only complaint about his plan is Planstin MEC requires PHCS and in MN there aren''t many  in-network providers but he was very happy with the way the MCS w/Zion worked and saved him a lot of money with his daughter''s thumb surgery and treatment.  Would have cost him approx. $8000 vs. $2500 he paid for his IUA. I asked him if he would do a video chat commentary with me and he said yes.  I told him I would schedule a time for it w/him.
Thomas said he needs his HSA.  I told him about ARM (that they are more open to working with members who have a hard time w/in-network providers), so he decided to stay with his SECURE HSA plan w/Zion and ARM.  I gave him the 2025 pricing for this plan - $658. I told him I would find out if he had to submit a change form or not for ARM and let him know.
Patti confirmed Thomas does not need to submit a change form. He will automatically be changed to the new SECURE HSA plan w/Zion-ARM combo and will be charged the 2025 pricing ($658) with the 12/20/24 billing.
